WEBVTT

1
00:00:38.115 --> 00:00:40.284
<i>Spotted offshore of Haneda Airport.</i>

2
00:00:40.368 --> 00:00:42.954
<i>We've got a pleasure craft adrift
in the open.</i>

3
00:00:43.037 --> 00:00:44.538
Hamanami. Roger that.

4
00:00:44.622 --> 00:00:46.332
Pleasure craft confirmed.

5
00:00:46.415 --> 00:00:48.793
No apparent hull damage.

6
00:00:48.876 --> 00:00:50.753
The <i>Glory-Maru.</i>

7
00:00:50.836 --> 00:00:54.215
MJG-15041.

8
00:00:54.298 --> 00:00:56.050
Requesting owner information.

9
00:00:57.134 --> 00:00:58.719
Boarding the vessel.

10
00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.849
Hello? Is anyone here?

11
00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:06.560
No one on the top deck!

12
00:01:06.644 --> 00:01:08.604
No signs of life.

13
00:01:08.688 --> 00:01:10.815
Just some personal effects.

14
00:01:12.233 --> 00:01:14.110
No traces of an incident.

15
00:01:14.193 --> 00:01:16.279
Perhaps they fell overboard?

16
00:01:17.989 --> 00:01:21.492
The vessel's vacant. We'll prepare a tow.

17
00:01:32.336 --> 00:01:34.005
Huh? What is that?

18
00:01:34.088 --> 00:01:35.589
Whoa. whoa. Wait. Wait. wait. wait!

19
00:01:40.428 --> 00:01:42.722
The report came in
from Intelligence and Research.

20
00:01:42.805 --> 00:01:45.725
There's flooding in the Aqua-Line tunnel
due to a crack in the ceiling.

21
00:01:45.808 --> 00:01:49.061
Water's currently pouring onto
the auto lanes and trapping vehicles.

22
00:01:49.145 --> 00:01:51.439
I've gotten word that a liaison office
is up and running.

23
00:01:51.522 --> 00:01:53.024
and an emergency order
has already been issued.

24
00:01:53.107 --> 00:01:54.525
And the Prime Minister?

25
00:01:54.608 --> 00:01:56.402
Scheduled to arrive in 28 minutes.

26
00:01:56.485 --> 00:01:58.779
- We need intel now. Let's head downstairs.
- Right.

27
00:02:00.781 --> 00:02:03.617
<i>First report confirmed at about 8:30 a.m.</i>

28
00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:07.496
<i>Leak in the Tokyo Aqua-Line tunnel.
near the 2.5 kilo marker.</i>

29
00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:08.789
<i>Seawater entering from a fissure...</i>

30
00:02:08.873 --> 00:02:10.541
- Keep me updated as you get new info.
- Right.

31
00:02:10.624 --> 00:02:13.002
<i>Several cars trapped
and damaged by the flood.</i>

32
00:02:13.085 --> 00:02:15.171
<i>Emergency crews are currently
on the scene.</i>

33
00:02:15.254 --> 00:02:17.256
Several Hamanami Coast Guard personnel

34
00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:20.009
were caught in the steam cloud
that's rising in the bay.

35
00:02:20.092 --> 00:02:22.178
The Aqua-Line has been shut down
in both directions.

36
00:02:22.261 --> 00:02:25.514
The Coast Guard has issued safety alerts
throughout the region.

37
00:02:25.598 --> 00:02:27.850
What's the situation. Mr. Koriyama?

38
00:02:27.933 --> 00:02:31.187
A total of five collisions in the tunnel
have been confirmed so far.

39
00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:33.314
Do we know if it was an earthquake
that caused the flooding?

40
00:02:33.397 --> 00:02:35.066
We haven't received
the seismic readings yet.

41
00:02:35.149 --> 00:02:37.068
Is there any correlation between this
and the sea eruption?

42
00:02:37.151 --> 00:02:39.487
With limited info. we can't say for sure.

43
00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.072
We've just received aerial footage.

44
00:02:43.741 --> 00:02:46.911
So. it really is just an underwater
volcanic eruption then?

45
00:02:46.994 --> 00:02:49.413
That's not a normal eruption.

46
00:02:49.497 --> 00:02:51.165
<i>This is Coast Guard 691.</i>

47
00:02:51.248 --> 00:02:53.626
<i>reporting continued steam eruptions
in the bay.</i>

48
00:02:53.709 --> 00:02:55.753
<i>The churning water prevents
undersea visibility.</i>

49
00:02:55.836 --> 00:02:57.922
<i>so the situation underwater
cannot be confirmed.</i>

50
00:02:58.005 --> 00:02:59.090
The situation's unpredictable.

51
00:02:59.173 --> 00:03:00.883
What we need is a unified response.

52
00:03:00.966 --> 00:03:03.344
Let's put our heads together
and reorganize.

53
00:03:03.427 --> 00:03:04.428
<i>The former liaison office</i>

54
00:03:04.512 --> 00:03:06.555
<i>is now the Prime Minister's
response office.</i>

55
00:03:06.639 --> 00:03:08.682
<i>The FDMA disaster task force
has been established.</i>

56
00:03:08.766 --> 00:03:10.434
<i>3rd Regional
Coast Guard has sealed the bay.</i>

57
00:03:10.518 --> 00:03:12.186
<i>No sea or air access.</i>

58
00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:14.730
<i>The MLIT has notified residents
in the nearby coastal areas</i>

59
00:03:14.814 --> 00:03:16.107
<i>that they should evacuate.</i>

60
00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.275
<i>An evacuation advisory has been issued.</i>

61
00:03:18.359 --> 00:03:19.652
<i>Please evacuate the premises immediately.</i>

62
00:03:19.735 --> 00:03:21.320
<i>Follow police instructions.</i>

63
00:03:21.404 --> 00:03:24.698
<i>For your own safety.
board the train headed towards Kisarazu.</i>

64
00:03:24.782 --> 00:03:26.283
Water's still pouring in.
It's dangerous.

65
00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:27.910
What should I do about my car?

66
00:03:27.993 --> 00:03:29.328
This way. and watch your head
on the way down.

67
00:03:29.412 --> 00:03:30.579
Oh. cool. a slide.

68
00:03:30.663 --> 00:03:32.206
- Whoa!
- What's going on?

69
00:03:32.289 --> 00:03:33.332
Remain calm.

70
00:03:33.416 --> 00:03:34.917
<i>We're heading
to the first aid station now.</i>

71
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.210
- This place is kind of sick.
- If you're able to walk.

72
00:03:36.293 --> 00:03:37.878
- please do so.
- I don't want to. My feet hurt.

73
00:03:37.962 --> 00:03:40.464
<i>This is awesome.
Getting the scoop before anyone else.</i>

74
00:03:40.548 --> 00:03:42.007
<i>Can you come over here for a moment?</i>

75
00:03:43.342 --> 00:03:44.885
- Wait. wait. wait.
- What is that?

76
00:03:44.969 --> 00:03:45.970
- What?
- What's that noise?

77
00:03:46.053 --> 00:03:47.138
Ah. seems like something's up there.

78
00:03:47.221 --> 00:03:49.140
<i>Departing planes will return
to the terminal for now.</i>

79
00:03:49.223 --> 00:03:50.307
- This is bad.
<i>- Please stay calm and seat...</i>

80
00:03:50.391 --> 00:03:52.768
This is seriously starting
to freak me out.

81
00:03:52.852 --> 00:03:54.603
Huh? What's that?

82
00:03:54.687 --> 00:03:55.980
There's something there.

83
00:03:58.149 --> 00:03:59.900
Sir. the Prime Minister has returned.

84
00:03:59.984 --> 00:04:01.277
Therefore. the cause
of the Aqua-Line rupture

85
00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.611
is still under investigation.

86
00:04:02.695 --> 00:04:04.447
Never mind the details.

87
00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.824
- Were there any fatalities or not?
- None.

88
00:04:06.907 --> 00:04:08.784
Then just let the guys below deal with it.

89
00:04:08.868 --> 00:04:11.454
We can't.
There's secondary disaster risk after all.

90
00:04:11.537 --> 00:04:13.205
I've canceled your meeting
with the Secretary General

91
00:04:13.289 --> 00:04:15.541
so you can attend the briefing
that begins in five minutes.

92
00:04:15.624 --> 00:04:17.293
I see. Understood.

93
00:04:17.376 --> 00:04:20.713
This event indicates the presence of
some kind of undersea thermal discharge.

94
00:04:20.796 --> 00:04:22.923
but can anyone provide a possible cause?

95
00:04:23.007 --> 00:04:26.010
How about an unidentified nuclear
submarine accident. or a meltdown?

96
00:04:26.093 --> 00:04:30.222
In the bay? It's shallow and not suited
to larger vessels. let alone a submarine.

97
00:04:30.306 --> 00:04:32.975
We think the water was heated by magma
to cause a kind of vapor explosion.

98
00:04:33.058 --> 00:04:36.020
In other words. a new undersea
volcanic eruption is likely the cause.

99
00:04:36.103 --> 00:04:38.022
Uh. Mr. Yanagihara.

100
00:04:38.105 --> 00:04:40.399
It looks like the epicenter
of the explosion is shallow.

101
00:04:40.483 --> 00:04:42.902
and the ejecta are allegedly
just water vapor.

102
00:04:42.985 --> 00:04:45.863
therefore this can't technically
be recognized as volcanic.

103
00:04:45.946 --> 00:04:48.240
You didn't think
to share that info sooner?

104
00:04:48.324 --> 00:04:49.533
Forgive me.

105
00:04:49.617 --> 00:04:52.411
What if it was a large hydrothermal vent
that appeared out of nowhere?

106
00:04:52.495 --> 00:04:53.746
That's good. I like that theory.

107
00:04:53.829 --> 00:04:56.040
However.
it's located directly above the tunnel.

108
00:04:56.123 --> 00:04:57.917
A vent in a location
that's been geologically surveyed

109
00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.251
would be hard to believe.

110
00:04:59.335 --> 00:05:01.212
So it's an oversight.
That's not unheard of.

111
00:05:01.295 --> 00:05:03.130
Prime Minister...

112
00:05:03.214 --> 00:05:05.174
the seafloor...
there is something's on the seafloor.

113
00:05:05.257 --> 00:05:07.384
There's something? Like what?

114
00:05:07.468 --> 00:05:08.969
A giant creature's my assumption.

115
00:05:09.053 --> 00:05:10.971
There's even footage of it
you can look up online.

116
00:05:11.055 --> 00:05:13.974
Preposterous. Are you saying this thing
is just a big whale spouting?

117
00:05:14.058 --> 00:05:15.476
The seawater is boiling.

118
00:05:15.559 --> 00:05:17.770
There's no creature with a body
temperature over a hundred degrees.

119
00:05:17.853 --> 00:05:20.564
We've been scouring online videos as well.
Prime Minister.

120
00:05:20.648 --> 00:05:24.318
We've yet to find any conclusive evidence
as to what caused the flooding.

121
00:05:24.401 --> 00:05:26.445
We're wasting time here. so let's do this.

122
00:05:26.529 --> 00:05:28.531
Why don't we focus
on narrowing down our choices?

123
00:05:28.614 --> 00:05:32.701
That's right. So we have a new undersea
volcano or a large hydrothermal vent.

124
00:05:32.785 --> 00:05:34.286
There's nothing else it could be.

125
00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:36.830
Then next on our list is not only
putting together a basic response.

126
00:05:36.914 --> 00:05:39.291
we should also gather the relevant
cabinet ministers for a meeting.

127
00:05:39.375 --> 00:05:41.001
Will that be sufficient?

128
00:05:41.085 --> 00:05:43.420
Right. Good idea.

129
00:05:43.504 --> 00:05:47.091
In that case. let's move to
the main conference room. everyone.

130
00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:54.515
We have to stay on top of this situation.

131
00:05:54.598 --> 00:05:56.225
Yaguchi.

132
00:05:57.393 --> 00:06:00.604
Everything's set so all you can do now
is toe the line on their decision.

133
00:06:00.688 --> 00:06:02.481
Don't stir things up. you got that?

134
00:06:02.565 --> 00:06:05.401
I just think we should consider
every single possibility there is.

135
00:06:05.484 --> 00:06:07.027
I get that you're rebellious.

136
00:06:07.111 --> 00:06:10.322
but think of the position of the guy
who recommended you.

137
00:06:10.406 --> 00:06:13.075
A warning. Do what you will with it.

138
00:06:18.831 --> 00:06:21.375
The transportation of all those injured
has been completed

139
00:06:21.458 --> 00:06:22.668
and they're receiving care.

140
00:06:22.751 --> 00:06:25.337
Fireboats and information-gathering
helicopters have been dispatched

141
00:06:25.421 --> 00:06:27.548
to Tokyo Bay and stand ready to respond.

142
00:06:27.631 --> 00:06:30.092
We're prepared for any situation.
That's all.

143
00:06:30.175 --> 00:06:32.970
Regarding the coastal region
of Tokyo Bay.

144
00:06:33.053 --> 00:06:36.098
Due to the risk of damage from debris
and ash caused by the eruption.

145
00:06:36.181 --> 00:06:38.392
we've begun evacuation preparations.

146
00:06:38.475 --> 00:06:41.103
and we're grounding all flights
out of Haneda Airport.

147
00:06:41.186 --> 00:06:44.231
We're taking thorough
crisis management measures.

148
00:06:48.319 --> 00:06:51.071
Forgive me. An addendum.

149
00:06:51.155 --> 00:06:54.575
Uh... The grounding of all flights
out of Haneda

150
00:06:54.658 --> 00:07:00.080
is a necessary measure to prioritize
citizen safety over any economic losses.

151
00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:03.334
We've deduced that a new undersea volcano

152
00:07:03.417 --> 00:07:05.753
is believed to be the cause
of the tunnel flooding accident.

153
00:07:05.836 --> 00:07:09.840
Fortunately. not a single trace
of toxic gases has been detected so far.

154
00:07:09.923 --> 00:07:13.010
We're sending research teams from
both the Meteorological Agency

155
00:07:13.093 --> 00:07:15.054
and the Coast Guard
to investigate the site.

156
00:07:15.137 --> 00:07:19.642
They'll conduct a thorough investigation
there and report back as soon as possible.

157
00:07:22.561 --> 00:07:24.146
Oh.

158
00:07:24.229 --> 00:07:26.106
Everyone. we've just received a report

159
00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:28.525
that eruption activity
is dying down rapidly.

160
00:07:28.609 --> 00:07:30.402
That's good.

161
00:07:35.407 --> 00:07:36.909
Does that mean it's over?

162
00:07:36.992 --> 00:07:38.410
Mm. guess it was nothing

163
00:07:38.494 --> 00:07:41.246
Prime Minister.
I must reiterate something.

164
00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:45.668
It's still possible that the cause of
the accident is a giant marine creature.

165
00:07:45.751 --> 00:07:47.169
I'd like everyone here to consider this.

166
00:07:47.252 --> 00:07:50.005
Yaguchi. this is a cabinet meeting.
No place for jokes.

167
00:07:50.089 --> 00:07:52.716
Everything's going on record.
Do you want to embarrass us?

168
00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:54.343
There is no such marine creature!

169
00:08:03.394 --> 00:08:04.687
And that's to be as expected.

170
00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:06.271
No time frame for restoration
or prospect or recovery means...

171
00:08:06.355 --> 00:08:07.481
- Sir?
- Hmm?

172
00:08:07.564 --> 00:08:09.233
There's been another incident.
You should turn on the TV.

173
00:08:09.316 --> 00:08:10.776
...expect those losses to continue
to increase in the future.

174
00:08:10.859 --> 00:08:13.362
Sorry. We have to delay
this discussion for now.

175
00:08:13.445 --> 00:08:16.115
The television. Turn on the TV now.

176
00:08:17.199 --> 00:08:18.450
<i>This is unbelievable!</i>

177
00:08:18.534 --> 00:08:19.910
<i>I've never seen anything like it!</i>

178
00:08:20.703 --> 00:08:24.123
<i>We've captured footage of an object that
suddenly breached the surface of the sea</i>

179
00:08:24.206 --> 00:08:25.249
<i>and stretched into the sky!</i>

180
00:08:25.332 --> 00:08:27.084
Wh-what could that be. do you think?

181
00:08:27.167 --> 00:08:29.461
- It could be..?
- It's definitely a tail.

182
00:08:29.545 --> 00:08:33.632
Yaguchi's joke is a serious matter
after all. wouldn't you say?

183
00:08:33.716 --> 00:08:36.844
Let us officially adjourn here
due to the change in situation.

184
00:08:36.927 --> 00:08:39.346
All relevant ministers should head
to the Prime Minister's office right away.

185
00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:41.014
<i>...from an Eyewitness News helicopter.</i>

186
00:08:44.101 --> 00:08:46.603
So. what is that?

187
00:08:46.687 --> 00:08:49.356
A Giant Unidentified Life-Form.
Prime Minister.

188
00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.817
Well. that's only what
we're calling it for now.

189
00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.278
But currently. uh. we're gathering
biologists and scholars

190
00:08:54.361 --> 00:08:55.904
from various fields.
which includes the ministry.

191
00:08:55.988 --> 00:08:58.198
as well as universities
and research institutes.

192
00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:00.868
We'll narrow down the candidates.
hold an emergency expert meeting

193
00:09:00.951 --> 00:09:03.162
to ascertain what this thing is
and what we should call it.

194
00:09:03.245 --> 00:09:04.455
We need to know right away.

195
00:09:04.538 --> 00:09:05.873
- Do all you can.
- Right.

196
00:09:05.956 --> 00:09:07.166
Prime Minister.

197
00:09:07.249 --> 00:09:09.042
We should concentrate

198
00:09:09.126 --> 00:09:11.086
our response to all this.
wouldn't you agree?

199
00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:12.171
Uh. yes. I do.

200
00:09:12.254 --> 00:09:15.340
However. this is way more unexpected
than we thought.

201
00:09:15.424 --> 00:09:18.177
Yet our choices for the response
are quite simple. I think.

202
00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:20.053
We can try to capture it
and exterminate it.

203
00:09:20.137 --> 00:09:21.764
Do what we can to drive it away.

204
00:09:21.847 --> 00:09:24.349
or we can choose to do nothing at all
and just let it go.

205
00:09:24.433 --> 00:09:26.477
In that case. I vote for extermination.

206
00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:28.437
And I concur.

207
00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:31.190
Setting aside the connection
to the tunnel accident for a minute.

208
00:09:31.273 --> 00:09:32.941
there's the closing of Tokyo Bay

209
00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:35.027
as well as the grounding
of all Haneda flights.

210
00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:37.905
so we're already looking at
huge economic losses.

211
00:09:37.988 --> 00:09:40.157
I agree. I vote to exterminate it.

212
00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:42.534
Me. too. We should get rid of it
as soon as possible.

213
00:09:42.618 --> 00:09:44.369
Right. Defense Minister?

214
00:09:44.453 --> 00:09:46.580
Uh...

215
00:09:46.663 --> 00:09:48.665
While there have been deployments
in the past

216
00:09:48.749 --> 00:09:51.001
for the purpose of exterminating
harmful animals.

217
00:09:51.084 --> 00:09:53.921
our forces have technically
never used firearms in Tokyo Bay.

218
00:09:54.004 --> 00:09:55.756
so we're unsure.

219
00:09:55.839 --> 00:09:57.633
Why murder it?
Can we not just get rid of it?

220
00:09:57.716 --> 00:09:59.134
Peacefully chase it off?

221
00:09:59.218 --> 00:10:00.260
Prime Minister.

222
00:10:00.344 --> 00:10:02.763
Environmental protection groups
and academic societies.

223
00:10:02.846 --> 00:10:04.848
several of them have weighed in
saying that the creature

224
00:10:04.932 --> 00:10:06.600
should be regarded as a new species.

225
00:10:06.683 --> 00:10:09.269
They want nets in the bay
so it can be captured alive.

226
00:10:09.353 --> 00:10:10.687
No. we have to kill it.

227
00:10:10.771 --> 00:10:12.564
Why don't we just use some torpedoes
or something?

228
00:10:12.648 --> 00:10:14.233
I understand your feelings on the matter.

229
00:10:14.316 --> 00:10:17.402
however. the sanctioned use of weapons
requires careful consideration.

230
00:10:17.486 --> 00:10:18.987
Out of our current options.

231
00:10:19.071 --> 00:10:22.282
I'd like to ask that you strongly consider
live capture.

232
00:10:22.366 --> 00:10:25.202
Start gathering information
on the giant unknown creature right now.

233
00:10:25.285 --> 00:10:26.662
Consider each case scenario.

234
00:10:26.745 --> 00:10:29.081
individual responses for its seizure.
removal and execution.

235
00:10:33.001 --> 00:10:34.878
Sorry. which of us were you talking to?

236
00:10:40.008 --> 00:10:42.761
It appears that a vapor cloud has started
moving towards the Tama River.

237
00:10:42.845 --> 00:10:44.847
Huh? It's moving?

238
00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:46.348
Well. it's alive. isn't it?

239
00:10:47.432 --> 00:10:50.686
<i>The giant unknown creature
is just off Haneda Airport near runway D.</i>

240
00:10:50.769 --> 00:10:53.021
<i>It's entering the Tama River.</i>

241
00:10:54.648 --> 00:10:57.734
We just got a report of flooding on
the Bayshore Expressway. Damage unknown.

242
00:10:57.818 --> 00:10:59.111
The hell is going on?

243
00:10:59.194 --> 00:11:00.779
Maybe don't capture it?

244
00:11:00.863 --> 00:11:02.739
Prime Minister.
three biologists have arrived.

245
00:11:02.823 --> 00:11:05.242
I recommend that we go
consult with them immediately.

246
00:11:16.253 --> 00:11:18.505
Hard to tell what it is
from the TV footage alone.

247
00:11:18.589 --> 00:11:21.425
Whether it's a dinosaur
or a subspecies of whale.

248
00:11:21.508 --> 00:11:23.886
We can't identify it with this footage.

249
00:11:25.178 --> 00:11:29.474
It seems to me that this creature
is a new aquatic species.

250
00:11:29.558 --> 00:11:33.145
Yet I can't say for certain
without examining the creature for myself.

251
00:11:34.354 --> 00:11:37.149
I'm concerned about whether or not
this footage is even real.

252
00:11:37.232 --> 00:11:42.654
If I made a judgment
that was based on unverified evidence...

253
00:11:42.738 --> 00:11:46.033
then I'd lose credibility as a biologist.

254
00:11:48.035 --> 00:11:49.578
The meeting's wrapping up.

255
00:11:49.661 --> 00:11:51.330
We'll resume in five minutes.

256
00:11:51.413 --> 00:11:53.415
This is getting ridiculous.

257
00:12:13.769 --> 00:12:15.187
What a waste of time that was.

258
00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:16.772
Those so-called experts were useless.

259
00:12:16.855 --> 00:12:18.941
- I agree.
- I couldn't care less about status.

260
00:12:19.024 --> 00:12:20.984
Just get someone who actually
knows something.

261
00:12:21.068 --> 00:12:22.444
Will do.

262
00:12:25.864 --> 00:12:27.240
- Shimura.
- Yes?

263
00:12:27.324 --> 00:12:28.575
Who can we call?

264
00:12:28.659 --> 00:12:31.036
I have a college friend over
at the Ministry of the Environment

265
00:12:31.119 --> 00:12:32.913
who would know about this.
but she's still low ranking.

266
00:12:32.996 --> 00:12:34.498
I don't mind. Call her right away.

267
00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:44.800
This creature. while it does walk.

268
00:12:44.883 --> 00:12:46.885
it looks like its default
is a snake-like movement.

269
00:12:46.969 --> 00:12:49.346
We can deduce that it's aquatic
judging by the shape of its gills.

270
00:12:49.429 --> 00:12:51.306
however. it also has legs like a lungfish.

271
00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:54.476
If this thing has legs.
is it possible it can come on land?

272
00:12:55.644 --> 00:12:57.354
Yes. It is a possibility.

273
00:12:57.437 --> 00:12:59.648
Is that true? What's going on?

274
00:12:59.731 --> 00:13:04.403
Well. frankly. we have yet to officially
decide which agency it falls under.

275
00:13:04.486 --> 00:13:06.822
Our scholar says
that even if it had finlike feet.

276
00:13:06.905 --> 00:13:09.199
an aquatic creature's internal organs
and bones would be unable to handle

277
00:13:09.282 --> 00:13:10.993
the full force of gravity on land.

278
00:13:11.076 --> 00:13:14.121
As a result. it would be crushed
by its own weight. so I think we're safe.

279
00:13:14.204 --> 00:13:15.414
I appreciate that assertion.

280
00:13:15.497 --> 00:13:17.124
however. I think it's already
supporting its own weight.

281
00:13:17.207 --> 00:13:18.333
Is that true?

282
00:13:18.417 --> 00:13:19.960
What do you think. Environment Minister?

283
00:13:20.043 --> 00:13:21.169
Uh. uh. yes.

284
00:13:21.253 --> 00:13:25.132
Uh. please forgive my Deputy Chief's
lack of decorum today.

285
00:13:25.215 --> 00:13:27.175
Just as your experts have
already concluded.

286
00:13:27.259 --> 00:13:30.012
I believe the creature coming on land
is very improbable.

287
00:13:30.095 --> 00:13:31.096
I see.

288
00:13:31.179 --> 00:13:35.183
Prime Minister. considering the extent
of the destruction so far.

289
00:13:35.267 --> 00:13:38.311
I recommend that we hold
an emergency press conference

290
00:13:38.395 --> 00:13:40.939
to calm the nation's citizens.
ideally as soon as possible.

291
00:13:41.023 --> 00:13:43.859
Not just that. During the conference.
it's crucial that we disclose

292
00:13:43.942 --> 00:13:47.154
only what is necessary. and clarify.
that it's verified information.

293
00:13:47.237 --> 00:13:48.822
Understood.

294
00:13:50.032 --> 00:13:51.867
Get my emergency response uniform.

295
00:14:12.846 --> 00:14:15.849
The Giant Unidentified Life-Form
has caused significant damage

296
00:14:15.932 --> 00:14:18.018
to both the Aqua-Line
and Tama River tunnels.

297
00:14:18.101 --> 00:14:22.814
It's currently migrating up
the Nomi River in Ota Ward.

298
00:14:22.898 --> 00:14:26.151
While we've yet to identify
what sort of creature it is.

299
00:14:26.234 --> 00:14:28.612
<i>we don't expect it
to ever come out of the water.</i>

300
00:14:28.695 --> 00:14:29.988
<i>Even if it were to beach itself.</i>

301
00:14:30.072 --> 00:14:33.575
<i>we think that by the time it reaches the
shallow water. it'll likely be crushed.</i>

302
00:14:33.658 --> 00:14:36.953
<i>The creature would be crushed to death
under its own weight.</i>

303
00:14:37.037 --> 00:14:40.791
<i>I repeat. there's no immediate danger
of the creature coming ashore.</i>

304
00:14:40.874 --> 00:14:44.586
<i>So beloved citizens of Tokyo.
I ask that you set your minds at ease.</i>

305
00:14:44.669 --> 00:14:46.755
<i>Prime Minister.
please excuse the interruption.</i>

306
00:14:47.839 --> 00:14:49.424
Sir. the creature has come on shore.</i>

307
00:14:49.508 --> 00:14:51.134
Huh?! Are you sure?

308
00:15:06.483 --> 00:15:08.110
What was the point?

309
00:15:08.193 --> 00:15:10.445
You said there was no immediate danger.

310
00:15:10.529 --> 00:15:11.696
What do we do now?

311
00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:13.615
I just lied on national television.

312
00:15:13.698 --> 00:15:15.534
That's why we asked that you
please not change the wording

313
00:15:15.617 --> 00:15:17.285
or go off script and just read it as is.

314
00:15:17.369 --> 00:15:18.870
I needed to reassure the public.

315
00:15:18.954 --> 00:15:20.205
That's what a good leader does.

316
00:15:20.288 --> 00:15:21.498
You're right. of course.

317
00:15:21.581 --> 00:15:22.833
We're waiting to hear back
from our experts

318
00:15:22.916 --> 00:15:24.084
on how the creature made landfall.

319
00:15:24.167 --> 00:15:25.502
I don't care about that.

320
00:15:25.585 --> 00:15:26.586
What's the current situation?

321
00:15:47.899 --> 00:15:49.609
Prime Minister.
I strongly suggest we arrange

322
00:15:49.693 --> 00:15:51.903
an emergency disaster control
headquarters right away.

323
00:15:51.987 --> 00:15:53.113
Then do it.

324
00:15:53.196 --> 00:15:56.783
This cabinet meeting
is now officially adjourned.

325
00:15:56.867 --> 00:15:59.035
Well. everyone. that's all for now.

326
00:16:00.453 --> 00:16:02.330
We want to get rid of
all these formal meetings.

327
00:16:02.414 --> 00:16:04.374
but we have to have a meeting
in order to do that.

328
00:16:04.457 --> 00:16:06.334
Yes. it's inefficient.
but it's all for documentation.

329
00:16:06.418 --> 00:16:07.794
which is democracy's foundation.

330
00:16:07.878 --> 00:16:10.463
Still. we can't even hold a press
conference without having to go all out.

331
00:16:10.547 --> 00:16:13.758
<i>Regarding the Giant Unidentified Life-Form
that has landed in Tokyo.</i>

332
00:16:13.842 --> 00:16:17.095
<i>the government has established an
emergency disaster control headquarters</i>

333
00:16:17.179 --> 00:16:19.848
<i>for the sole purpose of combating it.</i>

334
00:16:19.931 --> 00:16:22.309
<i>We are crafting a full-scale response
to ensure that all possible measures</i>

335
00:16:22.392 --> 00:16:24.477
<i>are taken to ensure the safety
of the people.</i>

336
00:16:24.561 --> 00:16:28.273
<i>This includes being in close contact
with Tokyo and federal government agencies</i>

337
00:16:28.356 --> 00:16:31.234
<i>in order to carry out
a coordinated evacuation.</i>

338
00:16:31.318 --> 00:16:32.527
<i>Furthermore...</i>

339
00:16:40.827 --> 00:16:43.663
<i>The Giant Unidentified Life-Form
is currently heading to Shinagawa Ward.</i>

340
00:16:43.747 --> 00:16:46.416
<i>We're clocking its average speed at about
13 kilometers per hour.</i>

341
00:16:46.499 --> 00:16:49.085
For something so large.
it moves very slowly.

342
00:16:49.169 --> 00:16:51.880
Even so. it could trample through the
whole capital in three hours at this pace.

343
00:16:51.963 --> 00:16:54.549
I guess Tokyo's surprisingly small
and fragile.

344
00:16:54.633 --> 00:16:55.634
This is bad.

345
00:16:55.717 --> 00:16:57.427
We are looking at catastrophic damage.

346
00:16:57.510 --> 00:16:59.346
That's why we need
to exterminate it already.

347
00:16:59.429 --> 00:17:01.223
It's a densely-populated part of the city.

348
00:17:01.306 --> 00:17:03.391
Evacuations of the citizens should
really take priority.

349
00:17:03.475 --> 00:17:06.436
The MIC and the MLIT need
to start working on evacuation zones

350
00:17:06.519 --> 00:17:08.188
and transportation methods.

351
00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:12.400
<i>We've received orders
from the Prime Minister</i>

352
00:17:12.484 --> 00:17:15.195
<i>to conduct evacuation measures.
possibly shadow evacuation.</i>

353
00:17:15.278 --> 00:17:17.239
Why didn't they issue an evacuation order
right away?

354
00:17:17.322 --> 00:17:18.782
This is unprecedented.

355
00:17:18.865 --> 00:17:20.992
Nothing in the first response manual
applies here.

356
00:17:21.076 --> 00:17:22.827
The first response manual
has always been useless.

357
00:17:22.953 --> 00:17:25.205
That case. you draft an order on the fly.

358
00:17:25.288 --> 00:17:26.998
We haven't undergone any
disaster prevention training

359
00:17:27.082 --> 00:17:28.333
for an event like this.

360
00:17:28.416 --> 00:17:32.545
And if we want to avoid nationwide panic.
do not call for a wide evacuation area.

361
00:17:32.629 --> 00:17:35.548
The city residents are gonna have
to evacuate themselves.

362
00:17:35.632 --> 00:17:37.926
We'll give it our all
to control traffic at the scene

363
00:17:38.009 --> 00:17:39.219
to get everyone out efficiently.

364
00:17:39.302 --> 00:17:41.680
<i>This traffic light is out of order.</i>

365
00:17:41.763 --> 00:17:43.640
<i>Please leave your vehicles immediately.</i>

366
00:17:43.723 --> 00:17:46.559
<i>Follow the instructions of the police
and other safety personnel.</i>

367
00:17:46.643 --> 00:17:48.436
<i>Attention.</i>

368
00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:50.355
<i>The Tokyo Metropolitan Government</i>

369
00:17:50.438 --> 00:17:54.067
<i>has ordered the full evacuation
of Shinagawa Ward.</i>

370
00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:57.237
<i>All residents are required
to quickly evacuate the area.</i>

371
00:18:17.674 --> 00:18:19.509
Honey. we have to get going!

372
00:18:37.444 --> 00:18:40.280
At this rate. the city will be in ruins.

373
00:18:40.363 --> 00:18:43.199
We need to contact the NPSC.

374
00:18:43.283 --> 00:18:44.909
If the federal government doesn't act.

375
00:18:44.993 --> 00:18:46.745
then we'll have to request
the Self-Defense Forces

376
00:18:46.828 --> 00:18:48.580
to eradicate this thing for our security.

377
00:18:48.663 --> 00:18:50.415
They want to use weapons?

378
00:18:50.498 --> 00:18:53.501
If they do. we interpret this
as an armed attack under Article 76.

379
00:18:53.585 --> 00:18:55.795
then a defense mobilization
allows the use of force.

380
00:18:55.879 --> 00:18:57.964
This doesn't technically qualify
as an armed attack.

381
00:18:58.089 --> 00:19:01.009
Article 76 stipulates the case
of the attacker as a foreign nation

382
00:19:01.092 --> 00:19:03.011
or something equivalent.
which means this doesn't count.

383
00:19:03.094 --> 00:19:04.220
Monsters don't count.

384
00:19:04.304 --> 00:19:06.639
I'm sure you're aware that wording
is the least of our concerns.

385
00:19:06.723 --> 00:19:09.225
No matter how you look at it.
only the SDF can deal with this.

386
00:19:09.309 --> 00:19:12.729
But that would mean soldiers engaging
in a battle in the city.

387
00:19:12.812 --> 00:19:15.482
Well. that'll certainly give
the Prime Minister pause.

388
00:19:17.359 --> 00:19:18.818
An integrated response.

389
00:19:18.902 --> 00:19:20.111
We need to integrate
all parts of our response

390
00:19:20.195 --> 00:19:23.615
including both deploying Self-Defense
Forces and citizen evacuation.

391
00:19:23.698 --> 00:19:26.409
That's why I think you should declare
a state of emergency. Prime Minister.

392
00:19:26.493 --> 00:19:29.037
It appears we're left with only one thing
we can do.

393
00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:31.748
Mobilization for defense
as an extralegal measure.

394
00:19:31.873 --> 00:19:34.626
However. only the Prime Minister can make
that decision.

395
00:19:34.709 --> 00:19:39.714
You're suggesting a proclamation
that has never been issued before. ever.

396
00:19:39.798 --> 00:19:43.551
In addition.
we'd be mobilizing our country for war.

397
00:19:43.635 --> 00:19:44.928
The evacuation.

398
00:19:45.011 --> 00:19:47.680
One of this size will undoubtedly
be difficult for police forces.

399
00:19:47.764 --> 00:19:49.557
Mobilizing defense has its risks.

400
00:19:49.641 --> 00:19:52.102
Consider the residents who aren't
able to flee in the middle of combat.

401
00:19:52.185 --> 00:19:53.686
which means collateral damage.

402
00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:55.146
No. no. Not that.

403
00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:56.898
How about the U.S. forces that are here?

404
00:19:56.981 --> 00:19:59.943
What if we have them take over killing
the creature under the Security Treaty?

405
00:20:00.026 --> 00:20:03.488
Our government and Self-Defense Forces
always have to take action first.

406
00:20:03.571 --> 00:20:07.409
Even under our Treaty. it states the U.S.
can only provide support.

407
00:20:07.492 --> 00:20:09.536
We're dealing with a living thing here.

408
00:20:09.619 --> 00:20:10.912
We don't know what it'll do.

409
00:20:10.995 --> 00:20:13.373
Irritating the creature could cause
even more damage.

410
00:20:13.456 --> 00:20:15.083
Yes. it's a living thing.

411
00:20:15.166 --> 00:20:17.460
Therefore. eradicating it should
be achievable.

412
00:20:17.544 --> 00:20:19.379
Don't think of it like an earthquake
or typhoon.

413
00:20:19.462 --> 00:20:21.589
because unlike a natural disaster.
we can stop it.

414
00:20:21.673 --> 00:20:22.674
The citizens.

415
00:20:22.757 --> 00:20:24.467
Shouldn't protecting them come first?

416
00:20:24.551 --> 00:20:27.011
Prime Minster. we're aware that
this is a difficult decision.

417
00:20:27.095 --> 00:20:29.431
yet in order to avoid the damage
from spreading.

418
00:20:29.514 --> 00:20:31.891
your authorization is what's needed
right now.

419
00:20:31.975 --> 00:20:33.977
You mean right now decide?

420
00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:35.228
You're not serious?

421
00:20:35.311 --> 00:20:37.564
There's no more time. Your decision.

422
00:20:37.647 --> 00:20:40.984
<i>The Prime Minister has just declared
the first ever national state of emergency</i>

423
00:20:41.067 --> 00:20:43.486
<i>under the
Disaster Countermeasures Basic Act.</i>

424
00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:45.405
<i>The SDF's being summoned to defend.</i>

425
00:20:45.488 --> 00:20:49.117
<i>A first for Japan in reaction
to the Giant Unidentified Life-Form.</i>

426
00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:52.620
<i>As an emergency measure. Diet approval
has officially been postponed.</i>

427
00:20:52.704 --> 00:20:54.789
<i>For the first time since World War II.</i>

428
00:20:54.873 --> 00:20:58.501
<i>the Prime Minister has issued an order
for the elimination of harmful creatures.</i>

429
00:20:58.585 --> 00:21:01.963
<i>Nerima 1st Division has already
been dispatched at Tokyo's request.</i>

430
00:21:02.046 --> 00:21:03.381
Current operational units are tasked

431
00:21:03.465 --> 00:21:06.301
with evacuation guidance
and rescue missions.

432
00:21:06.384 --> 00:21:09.012
In any case.
they're not properly equipped for battle.

433
00:21:09.095 --> 00:21:11.181
Attack helicopters are the way
to go for now.

434
00:21:11.264 --> 00:21:12.640
We're still waiting on artillery.

435
00:21:12.724 --> 00:21:14.434
- Find out about Kisarazu.
- Yes. sir.

436
00:21:14.517 --> 00:21:16.644
Let's load the F-2s with incendiaries.
too. shall we?

437
00:21:16.728 --> 00:21:20.899
No. Any collateral damage could affect
the very survival of the SDF.

438
00:21:20.982 --> 00:21:22.609
We have to minimize the use of firepower.

439
00:21:22.692 --> 00:21:24.527
We still don't know
what this thing's capable of.

440
00:21:24.611 --> 00:21:27.572
I really think we need to be ready
to give it everything we've got.

441
00:21:27.655 --> 00:21:30.116
I agree. Let's advocate for an integrated.

442
00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:32.494
three-force operation
to the Joint Chiefs of Staff.

443
00:21:32.577 --> 00:21:33.912
Call the Prime Minister.

444
00:21:35.371 --> 00:21:38.875
They're proposing a joint task force with
the Eastern Army Commander as its leader.

445
00:21:38.958 --> 00:21:41.127
And the objective is extermination.

446
00:21:41.211 --> 00:21:45.006
The ground forces. they're prioritizing
evacuating residents and can't respond.

447
00:21:45.089 --> 00:21:49.344
Our main force will be made up of rapid
response helicopters. is what we propose.

448
00:21:49.427 --> 00:21:52.013
The city... this is an urban operation.

449
00:21:52.096 --> 00:21:54.682
There's a possibility
elderly and ill citizens may remain.

450
00:21:54.766 --> 00:21:58.144
Then I can't make any decisions
without checking the scene first.

451
00:21:58.228 --> 00:21:59.562
Under these conditions.
we believe collateral damage.

452
00:21:59.646 --> 00:22:00.980
including civilian casualties

453
00:22:01.064 --> 00:22:03.274
and destruction of private property.
is unavoidable.

454
00:22:03.358 --> 00:22:07.612
Prime Minister.
it's a difficult circumstance of course.

455
00:22:07.695 --> 00:22:09.781
Nevertheless. we need your answer.

456
00:22:10.907 --> 00:22:12.575
Understood.

457
00:22:16.621 --> 00:22:19.582
This is a risky. unprecedented mission
against an unknown enemy.

458
00:22:19.666 --> 00:22:20.959
Will anyone volunteer?

459
00:22:21.042 --> 00:22:22.418
No. standard rotation.

460
00:22:22.502 --> 00:22:25.296
This is what we signed up for.
every single one of us.

461
00:22:25.380 --> 00:22:27.549
Attention! Salute!

462
00:22:27.632 --> 00:22:29.676
<i>13:08.</i>

463
00:22:29.926 --> 00:22:32.679
<i>13:20. Over.</i>

464
00:22:37.767 --> 00:22:39.352
We can relax now.

465
00:22:39.435 --> 00:22:43.398
Even a creature of that size.
the SDF will make short work of it.

466
00:22:43.481 --> 00:22:46.442
Yeah. Hey. how about we see
if we can monetize the carcass

467
00:22:46.526 --> 00:22:47.735
to help rebuild the city.

468
00:22:47.819 --> 00:22:52.198
Minister. the old Imperial Army engaged
in wishful armchair theories.

469
00:22:52.323 --> 00:22:55.535
Those ideas. I know are appealing.
but the fact of the matter is

470
00:22:55.618 --> 00:22:58.454
that more than three million lives were
lost in the last war.

471
00:22:58.538 --> 00:23:00.790
so I'm warning against
having unfounded optimism.

472
00:23:10.049 --> 00:23:11.801
Hurry. hurry! Run!

473
00:23:15.054 --> 00:23:17.307
Please watch your step! Remain calm!

474
00:23:17.390 --> 00:23:20.018
Over here. this way! Let's go. quickly!

475
00:23:20.101 --> 00:23:22.520
Local evacuation centers are useless
to us right now.

476
00:23:22.604 --> 00:23:25.440
You got to tell us where
to send these people. Hurry!

477
00:23:48.171 --> 00:23:51.716
<i>The giant creature
appears to have suddenly stopped moving!</i>

478
00:23:51.799 --> 00:23:53.301
Stopped?

479
00:23:53.384 --> 00:23:54.594
Why all of sudden?

480
00:24:25.500 --> 00:24:27.043
Astounding.

481
00:24:28.628 --> 00:24:30.338
My God. it's evolving.

482
00:25:20.888 --> 00:25:23.182
<i>Attacker 1. this is CP. Over.</i>

483
00:25:23.266 --> 00:25:25.101
<i>CP. Attacker 1. Over.</i>

484
00:25:25.184 --> 00:25:28.229
<i>Advance to holding area two.
Await further orders. Over.</i>

485
00:25:28.312 --> 00:25:29.897
Attacker 1. Roger.

486
00:25:38.531 --> 00:25:40.199
The shape is different
from what was reported.

487
00:25:40.283 --> 00:25:41.701
CP. Attacker 1.

488
00:25:41.784 --> 00:25:43.119
The report was inaccurate.

489
00:25:43.202 --> 00:25:44.787
I repeat. the report was inaccurate.

490
00:25:44.871 --> 00:25:47.290
<i>Attacker 1. CP.
Proceeding with the operation.</i>

491
00:25:47.373 --> 00:25:49.417
<i>Stand by. Await instructions.</i>

492
00:25:50.418 --> 00:25:53.337
Evacuation of residents in
the operational area has concluded.

493
00:25:53.421 --> 00:25:54.547
Understood.

494
00:25:54.630 --> 00:25:57.175
Minister Hanamori.
we can open fire at any time now.

495
00:25:57.258 --> 00:25:58.384
Then let's proceed.

496
00:25:59.469 --> 00:26:01.304
We're ready. We'll fire on your command.

497
00:26:01.387 --> 00:26:02.638
Say the word.

498
00:26:03.723 --> 00:26:05.057
Very well.

499
00:26:05.141 --> 00:26:06.309
Go ahead.

500
00:26:06.392 --> 00:26:08.019
<i>Attacker 1. CP.</i>

501
00:26:08.102 --> 00:26:10.229
<i>Commence fire on the giant creature.</i>

502
00:26:10.313 --> 00:26:13.065
<i>Commence fire.
I repeat. commence fire. Over.</i>

503
00:26:13.941 --> 00:26:16.486
CP. Attacker 1. Roger that. Firing.

504
00:26:16.569 --> 00:26:17.987
<i>Target in sight.</i>

505
00:26:18.070 --> 00:26:19.197
<i>Aim straight for the head.</i>

506
00:26:19.280 --> 00:26:20.782
<i>300.</i>

507
00:26:20.823 --> 00:26:22.533
<i>Prepare to fire.</i>

508
00:26:22.617 --> 00:26:24.535
<i>Hold your fire! Hold your fire!</i>

509
00:26:36.047 --> 00:26:37.882
Why aren't they doing anything?

510
00:26:37.965 --> 00:26:39.550
<i>Civilians spotted near the line of fire.</i>

511
00:26:39.634 --> 00:26:40.718
Standing by. please advise.

512
00:26:41.886 --> 00:26:43.638
Civilians spotted!
Awaiting orders to fire!

513
00:26:43.721 --> 00:26:45.765
Civilians in sight.
awaiting orders to fire.

514
00:26:45.848 --> 00:26:47.642
Civilians in sight. awaiting orders
to fire.

515
00:26:47.725 --> 00:26:49.560
There are civilians present.

516
00:26:49.644 --> 00:26:51.312
Do we have permission to still open fire?

517
00:26:51.395 --> 00:26:53.064
What do we do? Should we fire?

518
00:26:53.147 --> 00:26:54.232
Your order?

519
00:26:55.483 --> 00:26:56.901
Prime Minister!

520
00:26:56.984 --> 00:26:58.820
Cancel the attack.

521
00:26:58.903 --> 00:27:00.530
Protect the civilians.

522
00:27:00.613 --> 00:27:03.241
None of them can be allowed to die
by our hand.

523
00:27:03.324 --> 00:27:05.326
<i>Attacker 1. CP. Abort attack.</i>

524
00:27:05.409 --> 00:27:06.994
<i>To holding positions. Over.</i>

525
00:27:07.078 --> 00:27:09.580
<i>Roger. Abort attack. Holding positions.</i>

526
00:27:27.139 --> 00:27:29.934
<i>The Giant Unidentified Life-Form has
left Tennozu Canal!</i>

527
00:27:30.017 --> 00:27:32.353
<i>It's broken through the expressway.
and is now moving</i>

528
00:27:32.436 --> 00:27:33.938
<i>from the Keihin Canal to Tokyo Bay!</i>

529
00:27:48.286 --> 00:27:49.954
<i>All flights in and out of Haneda Airport
have been canceled.</i>

530
00:27:50.037 --> 00:27:51.664
<i>There's been a new fire outbreak
near the Shinagawa Ward</i>

531
00:27:51.747 --> 00:27:53.207
<i>under the jurisdiction...</i>

532
00:27:53.291 --> 00:27:54.667
<i>All Tokyo train service operation
has resumed...</i>

533
00:27:54.750 --> 00:27:57.628
<i>Condolences and pledges of support
have been received...</i>

534
00:27:57.712 --> 00:28:00.256
<i>The Tokyo Metropolitan Government's
Disaster Prevention Division is in need</i>

535
00:28:00.339 --> 00:28:01.966
<i>- of more supplies and aid workers.
- The Tokyo Stock Exchange</i>

536
00:28:02.049 --> 00:28:03.926
<i>has announced that it'll continue
trading as usual...</i>

537
00:28:04.010 --> 00:28:06.137
<i>The Tokaido Shinkansen
is operating shuttle service</i>

538
00:28:06.220 --> 00:28:08.848
<i>- from Shin-Yokohama Station.
- Academic research teams</i>

539
00:28:08.931 --> 00:28:11.976
<i>from various countries.
including the United States and France.</i>

540
00:28:12.059 --> 00:28:14.020
<i>have landed at Narita
and Kansai Airports...</i>

541
00:28:14.103 --> 00:28:17.023
<i>The giant creature has yet to be spotted
in the Uraga Channel.</i>

542
00:28:17.106 --> 00:28:19.275
<i>As a result. the Yokosuka Naval District
of the MSDF</i>

543
00:28:19.358 --> 00:28:21.360
<i>has expanded the search area.</i>

544
00:28:21.444 --> 00:28:23.029
<i>They're now searching in Sagami Bay.</i>

545
00:28:23.112 --> 00:28:26.616
<i>The fires in both Ota Ward
and Shinagawa Ward have been put out.</i>

546
00:28:26.699 --> 00:28:29.994
<i>A government inspection team led
by Disaster Management Minister Kanai</i>

547
00:28:30.077 --> 00:28:33.915
<i>has been dispatched to directly survey
and assess the extent of the damage.</i>

548
00:28:38.461 --> 00:28:42.089
It was only on land for what.
a little over two hours?

549
00:28:42.173 --> 00:28:43.966
And look at this devastation.

550
00:28:44.050 --> 00:28:45.760
No.

551
00:28:45.843 --> 00:28:49.305
Even though it was two hours.
our response was inadequate.

552
00:28:49.388 --> 00:28:51.098
This is on us.

553
00:28:51.182 --> 00:28:53.768
It was an unforeseen incident.
Out of our control.

554
00:28:54.852 --> 00:28:58.439
We did the best we could.
given the circumstances. you know.

555
00:28:58.522 --> 00:29:00.816
Just don't get cocky.

556
00:29:00.900 --> 00:29:03.569
It's time to interview with the media.
Minister Kanai.

557
00:29:03.653 --> 00:29:04.946
This way. please.

558
00:29:05.029 --> 00:29:07.156
Okay. then.

559
00:29:35.685 --> 00:29:37.103
Helm. all ahead. Full.

560
00:29:37.186 --> 00:29:38.729
Aye. All ahead full.

561
00:29:38.813 --> 00:29:41.023
Ensure strict anti-submarine
and surface vigilance.

562
00:29:47.697 --> 00:29:50.408
We believe the Giant Unidentified
Life-Form has burrowed itself

563
00:29:50.491 --> 00:29:52.368
into Tokyo Bay near Kanaya.

564
00:29:52.451 --> 00:29:54.370
Currently. we've strengthened
our surveillance.

565
00:29:54.453 --> 00:29:58.290
The MSDF is at work patrolling
the coast of Chiba as well Sagami Bay.

566
00:29:58.374 --> 00:30:00.960
Though the Sagami Trough could
complicate things for us.

567
00:30:01.043 --> 00:30:02.628
I doubt we could detect it in there.

568
00:30:02.712 --> 00:30:05.506
So we don't know when
or where it will appear next?

569
00:30:06.882 --> 00:30:08.968
What do we do if it comes on land again?

570
00:30:11.178 --> 00:30:13.973
It'll be difficult to conduct a rapid land
strategy at the water's edge.

571
00:30:14.056 --> 00:30:15.850
We might not be able
to respond immediately.

572
00:30:15.933 --> 00:30:18.561
We need separate strategies
for a landing point encounter

573
00:30:18.644 --> 00:30:19.854
and an expeditionary pursuit

574
00:30:19.937 --> 00:30:22.023
so we can then use
first and second units accordingly.

575
00:30:22.106 --> 00:30:25.317
Right. We'll draw up strategies
with coordinated artillery. tank.

576
00:30:25.401 --> 00:30:28.112
and F-2 attacks in each and every scenario
for you to review.

577
00:30:28.195 --> 00:30:32.575
Still. defensive operations are
heavily concentrated in the Kanto region.

578
00:30:32.658 --> 00:30:35.286
Of course the metro area's defense
has to take top priority.

579
00:30:35.369 --> 00:30:37.872
Yeah. Sounds like an order
from the fifth floor.

580
00:30:37.955 --> 00:30:40.458
Does that mean they're just shelving
the other regions though?

581
00:30:40.541 --> 00:30:44.837
Tokyo has just over 13 million residents.
GNP of 85 trillion yen.

582
00:30:44.920 --> 00:30:47.339
which is 17% of the country's total.

583
00:30:47.423 --> 00:30:52.011
The Kanto region. on the other hand.
200 trillion yen. 40% of the total.

584
00:30:52.094 --> 00:30:55.598
It's a strategic decision intended
to safeguard the entire nation.

585
00:30:56.891 --> 00:30:59.060
I guess protecting the country is hard.

586
00:30:59.143 --> 00:31:01.145
We're leaving the defense plan
to headquarters

587
00:31:01.228 --> 00:31:03.564
and setting up a special response team
in the PM's residence.

588
00:31:03.647 --> 00:31:05.191
For the giant creature. right?

589
00:31:05.274 --> 00:31:07.610
You were appointed as bureau chief.
or so I was told.

590
00:31:07.693 --> 00:31:09.779
You got a promotion. Good for you.

591
00:31:09.862 --> 00:31:12.156
Aren't you the one who assigns
all the team members?

592
00:31:12.239 --> 00:31:14.283
Since you're friends
with all the bureaucrats.

593
00:31:14.366 --> 00:31:18.037
Understood. I'll bring you some people
I can trust who won't mince their words.

594
00:31:18.120 --> 00:31:20.289
Ah. Some people with balls.

595
00:31:20.372 --> 00:31:22.500
- I'm Tachikawa.
- I'm Takeo.

596
00:31:22.583 --> 00:31:24.126
- Ready. lift.
- Ready. lift.

597
00:31:37.223 --> 00:31:39.058
Everyone. my name is Rando Yaguchi.

598
00:31:39.141 --> 00:31:40.476
No matter what you do in this office.

599
00:31:40.559 --> 00:31:42.436
I assure you.
it won't affect your personnel evals.

600
00:31:42.520 --> 00:31:44.939
So don't worry about job titles
or seniority within the ministries.

601
00:31:45.022 --> 00:31:46.565
You should speak freely.

602
00:31:46.649 --> 00:31:48.150
Well. there you have it.

603
00:31:48.234 --> 00:31:49.485
I'll take over from here.

604
00:31:49.568 --> 00:31:52.113
This is a gathering of people who
are outcasts of the bureaucracy.

605
00:31:52.196 --> 00:31:54.824
Lone wolves. oddballs. nerds.
burdens. nuisances.

606
00:31:54.907 --> 00:31:56.534
troublemakers and academic heretics.

607
00:31:56.617 --> 00:31:59.120
We need you and your expertise.
so do what you do best.

608
00:31:59.203 --> 00:32:01.330
These are the creature's essential specs.

609
00:32:01.413 --> 00:32:03.916
Work together to find out what you can.

610
00:32:09.421 --> 00:32:10.548
Wait. that's all?

611
00:32:10.631 --> 00:32:13.217
Yes. that's all. So it's entirely up to us
to find the answer.

612
00:32:13.300 --> 00:32:15.845
If anyone else has further information.
share it.

613
00:32:15.928 --> 00:32:17.972
The experts yesterday couldn't
conclude anything.

614
00:32:18.055 --> 00:32:20.224
And to our dismay.
nothing of value was gained.

615
00:32:20.307 --> 00:32:22.143
all because they were at a loss
like the rest of us.

616
00:32:22.226 --> 00:32:24.311
I've outlined all of the creature's
configurations so far.

617
00:32:24.395 --> 00:32:27.022
Here's its first form.
its second form and its third form.

618
00:32:27.106 --> 00:32:28.607
It seems like more mutations are coming.

619
00:32:28.691 --> 00:32:29.733
More mutations?

620
00:32:30.943 --> 00:32:33.195
Also. we at RIKEN are currently analyzing
the fluid samples

621
00:32:33.279 --> 00:32:34.822
that were taken from the creature
the other day.

622
00:32:34.905 --> 00:32:37.867
Send some over when you can because I can
get outside facilities to help us out.

623
00:32:37.950 --> 00:32:39.160
Well. the U.S. already took the remaining

624
00:32:39.243 --> 00:32:41.287
creature bodily fluid samples.
unfortunately.

625
00:32:41.370 --> 00:32:43.122
Apparently. all the fluids left
at the scene were burned

626
00:32:43.205 --> 00:32:44.874
on the pretext that they smelled
of rot and decay.

627
00:32:44.957 --> 00:32:46.292
Uh-huh. that's right.

628
00:32:46.375 --> 00:32:48.169
And I hear the Americans were the ones
who wanted that.

629
00:32:48.252 --> 00:32:50.462
I'll leave the sample analysis
to RIKEN then.

630
00:32:50.546 --> 00:32:53.007
What else? What do we have
in Behavioral Biology findings?

631
00:32:53.090 --> 00:32:54.592
Only one behavioral pattern.

632
00:32:54.675 --> 00:32:56.260
All it really does is relocate

633
00:32:56.343 --> 00:32:57.887
so we can't determine
any sign of intellect.

634
00:32:57.970 --> 00:33:01.515
And it's probably unlikely that it has
the ability to communicate with us.

635
00:33:01.599 --> 00:33:03.225
I have a simple question.

636
00:33:03.309 --> 00:33:05.269
What is its source of energy?

637
00:33:05.352 --> 00:33:06.437
That's true.

638
00:33:06.520 --> 00:33:08.189
It requires a gigantic amount of energy.

639
00:33:08.272 --> 00:33:11.442
not just to get around but also
metabolically. now that I think about it.

640
00:33:11.525 --> 00:33:13.903
Oxygen conversion
in its digestive tract alone

641
00:33:13.986 --> 00:33:15.946
wouldn't be enough
for it to function properly.

642
00:33:16.030 --> 00:33:18.115
All of that energy...

643
00:33:21.118 --> 00:33:22.620
Is it nuclear fission?

644
00:33:23.495 --> 00:33:26.957
You can't be serious. Ms. Ogashira?

645
00:33:28.042 --> 00:33:29.168
Not possible.

646
00:33:32.296 --> 00:33:33.923
The U.S. carrier is leaving port?

647
00:33:34.006 --> 00:33:35.382
That's right.

648
00:33:35.466 --> 00:33:37.801
The alert went off
at Yokosuka's radiation monitoring post

649
00:33:37.885 --> 00:33:39.678
and we only received word of it just now.

650
00:33:39.762 --> 00:33:40.846
I understand.

651
00:33:40.930 --> 00:33:42.765
I'll check with
the Nuclear Regulation Authority.

652
00:33:42.848 --> 00:33:45.726
Uh. yes. I have orders to refrain
from announcing it to the public.

653
00:33:45.809 --> 00:33:49.355
however. an increase in radiation levels
has been observed all around Tokyo.

654
00:33:49.438 --> 00:33:51.398
So does that mean
there was a leak somewhere?

655
00:33:51.482 --> 00:33:52.691
Could it be a reactor?

656
00:33:52.775 --> 00:33:55.611
No. We haven't found any leaks
of radioactive materials

657
00:33:55.694 --> 00:33:57.529
at any of the nuclear facilities.

658
00:33:57.613 --> 00:33:59.657
If that's the case.
then what's the source?

659
00:34:03.786 --> 00:34:06.205
Is something like this
even possible?

660
00:34:06.288 --> 00:34:07.998
Huh?

661
00:34:09.458 --> 00:34:11.752
This survey data shows radiation spikes

662
00:34:11.835 --> 00:34:13.420
that are identical
to the giant creature's path.

663
00:34:13.504 --> 00:34:15.256
They're connected after all.

664
00:34:17.299 --> 00:34:18.968
Look at this.

665
00:34:20.094 --> 00:34:21.178
See?

666
00:34:24.723 --> 00:34:27.059
Looks like what Ms. Ogashira
said was right.

667
00:34:28.477 --> 00:34:29.728
I'm sorry.

668
00:34:39.780 --> 00:34:42.574
The information has already spread
quite a lot throughout the general public.

669
00:34:42.658 --> 00:34:43.867
Call Akasaka.

670
00:34:43.951 --> 00:34:46.078
I'll head to the
Chief Cabinet Secretary's office now.

671
00:34:48.622 --> 00:34:50.332
This is concerning.

672
00:34:50.416 --> 00:34:53.377
That's why you or the Prime Minister
should hold a news conference immediately.

673
00:34:53.460 --> 00:34:55.212
We haven't ID'd the radiation's source.

674
00:34:55.296 --> 00:34:58.257
and. furthermore. the link to the
aforementioned organism remains unclear.

675
00:34:58.340 --> 00:35:00.175
We'll stoke fear if we announce it now.

676
00:35:00.259 --> 00:35:03.387
The radiation level isn't high enough
for us to issue an evacuation.

677
00:35:03.470 --> 00:35:06.265
There are really no legal grounds for us
to act on this right now.

678
00:35:06.348 --> 00:35:09.059
However. this is still a matter
involving radioactive material.

679
00:35:09.143 --> 00:35:10.602
We should call a press conference.

680
00:35:10.686 --> 00:35:12.187
You're right.

681
00:35:12.271 --> 00:35:13.772
I'll see to it.

682
00:35:13.856 --> 00:35:16.233
I'll talk to the Prime Minister.

683
00:35:17.067 --> 00:35:18.444
A briefing.

684
00:35:18.527 --> 00:35:20.988
Schedule a briefing with
the Prime Minister in five minutes.

685
00:35:21.071 --> 00:35:22.781
Yes. President Ross.

686
00:35:22.823 --> 00:35:25.617
I understand. Thank you.

687
00:35:28.746 --> 00:35:31.832
So many requests from that country.

688
00:35:33.167 --> 00:35:35.252
That's the U.S. for you.

689
00:35:35.336 --> 00:35:38.672
An assistant deputy chief to the
U.S. President has secretly flown in.

690
00:35:38.756 --> 00:35:41.008
He wants to have an unofficial meeting
with the Prime Minister.

691
00:35:41.091 --> 00:35:42.468
Well. they certainly move fast.

692
00:35:42.551 --> 00:35:44.928
Yeah. He's left Yokota Air Base already.

693
00:35:45.012 --> 00:35:46.847
and he's on his way over here.
last I heard.

694
00:35:46.930 --> 00:35:49.266
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs
is going crazy.

695
00:35:49.350 --> 00:35:52.478
We've also received word
that his aide has made an appointment

696
00:35:52.561 --> 00:35:54.646
to talk with you while she's here.

697
00:35:54.730 --> 00:35:57.232
Me? Why's that?

698
00:35:57.316 --> 00:36:00.319
I read your current administration data
and decided on you.

699
00:36:00.402 --> 00:36:03.364
Your past is compelling.
and I figure you can be useful as well.

700
00:36:03.447 --> 00:36:05.032
Rando Yaguchi's the best choice overall.

701
00:36:05.115 --> 00:36:06.283
We're a great match.

702
00:36:06.367 --> 00:36:09.411
Well. I actually think Akasaka.

703
00:36:09.495 --> 00:36:11.038
the Prime Minister's aide.
would be better.

704
00:36:11.121 --> 00:36:14.166
Honestly. he turned it down so I chose you.

705
00:36:14.249 --> 00:36:17.628
I need something. and I need it
to look like I wasn't involved.

706
00:36:17.711 --> 00:36:20.339
What I need is for you to find
this person in question.

707
00:36:21.507 --> 00:36:23.842
Who are you trying to find?

708
00:36:24.927 --> 00:36:27.096
Several years ago.
there was a person who literally predicted

709
00:36:27.179 --> 00:36:29.348
your giant creature's sudden appearance.

710
00:36:29.431 --> 00:36:31.183
I bet that piqued your interest.

711
00:36:31.266 --> 00:36:34.353
The last update was that he landed
seven days ago in Narita.

712
00:36:34.436 --> 00:36:35.979
Goro Maki.

713
00:36:36.063 --> 00:36:37.773
Japanese.

714
00:36:37.856 --> 00:36:39.316
Former college professor.

715
00:36:39.400 --> 00:36:41.693
I hear your intelligence agency
is excellent.

716
00:36:41.777 --> 00:36:43.278
so don't fail.

717
00:36:43.362 --> 00:36:44.905
And what's in it for us?

718
00:36:47.741 --> 00:36:49.910
I'll trade all our info
for whatever you know.

719
00:36:49.993 --> 00:36:51.912
and then give you
our accumulated intelligence.

720
00:36:51.995 --> 00:36:55.457
However. no leaking intelligence
to a third country.

721
00:37:09.138 --> 00:37:10.139
Where's there a Zara?

722
00:37:10.222 --> 00:37:11.974
Kayoco Anne Patterson.

723
00:37:13.058 --> 00:37:14.476
She's very young.

724
00:37:14.560 --> 00:37:17.354
That country values performance over age.
which is a great quality.

725
00:37:17.438 --> 00:37:20.065
She's Senator Patterson's
eldest daughter as well.

726
00:37:20.149 --> 00:37:22.818
The child of the senator behind
the Kern Agreement then.

727
00:37:22.901 --> 00:37:24.445
She's a strong one.

728
00:37:24.528 --> 00:37:28.740
Her success is thanks to a mixture
of talent. pedigree. and coattail-riding.

729
00:37:28.824 --> 00:37:31.827
I'm guessing... she's not your type. huh?

730
00:37:31.910 --> 00:37:33.537
No.

731
00:37:33.620 --> 00:37:35.372
She has no shame.

732
00:37:35.456 --> 00:37:37.499
She uses her father's connection
to get ahead.

733
00:37:37.583 --> 00:37:40.961
She's just like Yaguchi.
a true politician.

734
00:37:43.881 --> 00:37:46.049
You're looking for someone
at a time like this?

735
00:37:46.133 --> 00:37:48.051
For Rando Yaguchi.

736
00:37:48.135 --> 00:37:51.013
I owe a great debt to his father.
so prioritize this.

737
00:37:51.096 --> 00:37:53.765
Assign however many agents you need.

738
00:37:53.849 --> 00:37:56.393
This is all the info we have.

739
00:37:58.103 --> 00:38:01.106
A heretical elderly professor
who was driven out of the country

740
00:38:01.190 --> 00:38:02.983
and transferred to a U.S. institute.

741
00:38:03.066 --> 00:38:05.986
Although a biologist.
it was an energy research institute

742
00:38:06.069 --> 00:38:07.446
that he was transferred to.

743
00:38:07.529 --> 00:38:08.864
Quite interesting. isn't it?

744
00:38:08.947 --> 00:38:10.782
Is this a red notice?

745
00:38:10.866 --> 00:38:13.368
No. Just locate his base of operations.

746
00:38:13.452 --> 00:38:17.456
After that. the NSA or the CIA
will take over for us.

747
00:38:17.539 --> 00:38:19.875
They told me
they'll get it done discreetly.

748
00:38:19.958 --> 00:38:21.627
The last traces of the former professor.

749
00:38:21.710 --> 00:38:25.005
As expected.
my grandma's country works fast.

750
00:38:25.088 --> 00:38:26.965
Unfortunately. he's gone missing.

751
00:38:27.049 --> 00:38:29.885
The Coast Guard found his little boat
adrift and unmanned

752
00:38:29.968 --> 00:38:31.178
off the coast of Haneda.

753
00:38:32.387 --> 00:38:34.765
Ms. Patterson.

754
00:38:34.848 --> 00:38:38.602
Was it really Goro Maki
you were looking for. or was it this?

755
00:38:40.729 --> 00:38:43.649
"I did what I wanted.
That means you should do the same."

756
00:38:44.733 --> 00:38:45.901
Is this a suicide note?

757
00:38:47.611 --> 00:38:48.820
Do you need me to confirm the contents?

758
00:38:52.449 --> 00:38:54.993
Printed with special ink.
It can't be copied.

759
00:38:55.077 --> 00:38:57.621
Then I'll take photos. They'll only be
shared with our response team.

760
00:39:00.374 --> 00:39:02.834
"God... zilla"?

761
00:39:09.401 --> 00:39:11.401
He chose to give it an English name.

762
00:39:11.426 --> 00:39:13.178
"Gojira."

763
00:39:13.262 --> 00:39:14.513
What's it mean?

764
00:39:15.681 --> 00:39:18.141
Looks like there's only one result.

765
00:39:18.225 --> 00:39:20.227
On Odo Island.
which was the guy's hometown.

766
00:39:20.310 --> 00:39:22.980
it's a word that means "God incarnate."

767
00:39:23.063 --> 00:39:24.398
A violent one.

768
00:39:24.481 --> 00:39:27.234
I hear that's why he wanted "God"
included in the English name.

769
00:39:27.317 --> 00:39:29.236
I don't like that.

770
00:39:29.319 --> 00:39:31.488
Let's stick to the Japanese pronunciation.

771
00:39:31.572 --> 00:39:33.907
Very well.

772
00:39:33.991 --> 00:39:35.450
Gojira.

773
00:39:35.534 --> 00:39:37.619
Who cares about the name right now?

774
00:39:37.703 --> 00:39:39.413
It doesn't matter.

775
00:39:39.496 --> 00:39:42.666
I think it's just as well
that it originated in the U.S.

776
00:39:42.749 --> 00:39:45.877
The important thing is now it has a name.

777
00:39:45.961 --> 00:39:48.171
<i>Just now.
the government unofficially announced</i>

778
00:39:48.255 --> 00:39:51.216
<i>that the giant creature will
be called Gojira.</i>

779
00:39:51.300 --> 00:39:53.969
<i>According to our sources. "God incarnate"
is the meaning.</i>

780
00:39:55.137 --> 00:39:56.847
Goro Maki.

781
00:39:56.930 --> 00:40:00.183
Former professor of integrative biology
at Jonan University.

782
00:40:01.685 --> 00:40:04.438
I want you to find out
what kind of person he was.

783
00:40:04.521 --> 00:40:08.066
We'll give it to you exclusively when
the time's right to go to print. Hayafune.

784
00:40:08.150 --> 00:40:10.235
That's a promise.

785
00:40:10.319 --> 00:40:12.362
I'll let you know
when we're ready for you.

786
00:40:12.446 --> 00:40:13.697
Yeah.

787
00:40:13.780 --> 00:40:15.616
I know you will.

788
00:40:20.495 --> 00:40:22.331
60 years ago.

789
00:40:22.414 --> 00:40:27.127
These are documents on the unregulated
dumping of radioactive waste in the ocean.

790
00:40:31.840 --> 00:40:33.342
Don't tell me...

791
00:40:33.425 --> 00:40:35.844
Gojira fed on these?

792
00:40:37.512 --> 00:40:39.723
That was the DOE's conclusion.

793
00:40:40.515 --> 00:40:43.060
The DOE noticed organisms that fed on
radioactive waste.

794
00:40:43.143 --> 00:40:45.354
and asked various institutions
to analyze them.

795
00:40:45.437 --> 00:40:47.981
Former professor Maki was the main figure
in all this.

796
00:40:48.065 --> 00:40:51.818
The radioactive waste was dumped in the
middle of an active marine life habitat.

797
00:40:51.902 --> 00:40:54.780
An organism from ancient times
that had miraculously survived.

798
00:40:54.863 --> 00:40:57.074
It didn't die out
due to radiation exposure.

799
00:40:57.157 --> 00:40:59.785
Instead. the organism evolved
to have radiation resistance.

800
00:41:01.203 --> 00:41:02.746
That was his theory for Godzilla.

801
00:41:02.829 --> 00:41:04.331
However. Ms. Patterson.

802
00:41:04.414 --> 00:41:07.000
the Gojira that arrived on land is clearly
longer than what was estimated.

803
00:41:07.084 --> 00:41:09.294
It has to do with its ability
to change

804
00:41:09.378 --> 00:41:11.296
from an aquatic to a terrestrial creature.

805
00:41:11.380 --> 00:41:13.632
It's beyond all of this info
that the DOE's given us.

806
00:41:13.715 --> 00:41:15.217
and I can't explain it either.

807
00:41:15.300 --> 00:41:18.178
I've officially told you everything
that I have the authority to know.

808
00:41:19.262 --> 00:41:20.764
So what now?

809
00:41:30.065 --> 00:41:31.066
- Hey!
- Huh?

810
00:41:31.149 --> 00:41:34.027
- So these were Professor Maki's then?

811
00:41:35.112 --> 00:41:36.822
I can't make sense of it.

812
00:41:39.032 --> 00:41:41.410
Well. it's definitely
not molecular geometry.

813
00:41:41.493 --> 00:41:43.120
How does it relate to Gojira?

814
00:41:43.203 --> 00:41:45.080
It's outside my field.
so I don't really understand it.

815
00:41:45.163 --> 00:41:47.040
but maybe an analytical table
of structural layers.

816
00:41:47.124 --> 00:41:49.084
It's missing data
that was intentionally left out

817
00:41:49.167 --> 00:41:51.253
so that no one who found it
could accurately analyze it.

818
00:41:51.336 --> 00:41:53.714
If we combine that with this.
we'll have the complete version.

819
00:41:53.797 --> 00:41:55.966
Do you mind if we analyze it as well?

820
00:41:56.049 --> 00:41:58.135
- Is that okay?

821
00:42:02.431 --> 00:42:04.725
I'm not really great
with Japanese formality.

822
00:42:04.808 --> 00:42:07.185
so can we speak casually?

823
00:42:08.145 --> 00:42:10.230
Then answer this.

824
00:42:10.313 --> 00:42:11.815
What does the U.S. want with Gojira?

825
00:42:11.898 --> 00:42:13.400
Will they study it or exterminate it?

826
00:42:13.483 --> 00:42:14.693
What are they planning?

827
00:42:14.776 --> 00:42:17.404
The one who decides that is the President.

828
00:42:19.614 --> 00:42:21.742
Who decides in your country?

829
00:42:26.705 --> 00:42:30.208
The Cabinet has finally decided
on a bill for relief and recovery?

830
00:42:30.292 --> 00:42:33.295
The Gojira-related bill is also difficult
to coordinate between the ministries.

831
00:42:33.378 --> 00:42:35.964
Orders are clouded right now since
it's such an unprecedented case.

832
00:42:36.047 --> 00:42:39.384
It's not exactly a shock that no one wants
to take responsibility right now.

833
00:42:39.468 --> 00:42:42.053
The bill on confidential info.
It passed easily at least. Yeah?

834
00:42:42.137 --> 00:42:44.681
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs forced it.
pressured by the U.S.. as usual.

835
00:42:44.765 --> 00:42:46.767
There's value in holding
all the knowledge. after all.

836
00:42:46.850 --> 00:42:49.853
U.S. wants to use its Gojira intel
as a diplomatic card in the future.

837
00:42:49.936 --> 00:42:51.188
We'll have to rely on Akasaka.

838
00:42:51.271 --> 00:42:53.857
He's crafty and good at negotiating.
he can handle the White House.

839
00:42:53.940 --> 00:42:55.692
Here are the analysis results
of the radioactive material

840
00:42:55.776 --> 00:42:57.068
recovered at the scene.

841
00:42:57.152 --> 00:42:59.988
The wavelength of these gamma rays
doesn't match those of existing ones.

842
00:43:00.071 --> 00:43:01.782
It's a huge discovery.

843
00:43:01.823 --> 00:43:03.200
Uh. Gojira. was it?

844
00:43:03.283 --> 00:43:06.661
There's a new. unknown element inside
of its body. that's what this means.

845
00:43:07.370 --> 00:43:09.915
So this is why the U.S.
and their Department of Energy

846
00:43:09.998 --> 00:43:12.584
took such quick action. huh?

847
00:43:12.667 --> 00:43:14.169
- Let's take this data with us.
- O-okay.

848
00:43:14.252 --> 00:43:15.962
- Call the Prime Minister.
- Sir.

849
00:43:16.046 --> 00:43:18.006
I understand.

850
00:43:18.089 --> 00:43:21.092
Radioactivity makes things
more complicated.

851
00:43:21.176 --> 00:43:22.844
So...

852
00:43:22.928 --> 00:43:25.096
how much do we say?

853
00:43:25.180 --> 00:43:27.474
<i>As a result of having fully
analyzed samples</i>

854
00:43:27.557 --> 00:43:29.810
<i>that were recovered
from along the path of Gojira.</i>

855
00:43:29.893 --> 00:43:34.481
<i>we were able to detect radiation
of 0.5 microsieverts in the area.</i>

856
00:43:34.564 --> 00:43:36.066
Thank you for the food.

857
00:43:36.149 --> 00:43:38.193
- Thank you for the food.
- Thanks.

858
00:43:38.276 --> 00:43:40.070
However. even though the U.S. gave us
all their information.

859
00:43:40.153 --> 00:43:41.488
now we're at a dead end.

860
00:43:41.571 --> 00:43:43.657
It feels like we're at a dead end
in several ways.

861
00:43:43.740 --> 00:43:46.451
I agree. although RIKEN's data
was impactful. after all.

862
00:43:46.535 --> 00:43:49.663
I never thought Gojira would have eight
times the genetic information of humans.

863
00:43:49.746 --> 00:43:52.874
We don't even know the number of years it
would take to sequence all of that info.

864
00:43:52.958 --> 00:43:54.209
This only verifies our suspicion

865
00:43:54.292 --> 00:43:57.003
that Gojira's the most evolved creature
on the entire planet.

866
00:43:57.087 --> 00:43:58.839
It doesn't evolve generationally.

867
00:43:58.922 --> 00:44:01.007
It self-mutates as a single individual.

868
00:44:01.091 --> 00:44:03.468
Perfection that exceeds even humans.

869
00:44:03.552 --> 00:44:05.345
Gojira's still a living thing.

870
00:44:05.428 --> 00:44:07.013
That means we can kill it.

871
00:44:07.097 --> 00:44:08.390
Well. that's our aim.

872
00:44:08.473 --> 00:44:11.935
Don't forget why we're all gathered here.
to find out how to defeat it.

873
00:44:12.018 --> 00:44:14.688
Has anyone found any clues into
its behavior while we're here?

874
00:44:14.771 --> 00:44:16.273
The only thing it does is walk.

875
00:44:16.356 --> 00:44:18.149
It went back to Tokyo Bay suddenly.

876
00:44:18.233 --> 00:44:20.151
Why do we think it decided to do that?

877
00:44:23.321 --> 00:44:25.198
I get it.

878
00:44:25.240 --> 00:44:26.658
To cool itself.

879
00:44:28.076 --> 00:44:30.829
Gojira likely has
a nuclear reactor-like system inside it.

880
00:44:30.912 --> 00:44:32.998
and from the dorsal fin.
the heat is released.

881
00:44:33.081 --> 00:44:34.666
However. that isn't enough on its own.

882
00:44:34.749 --> 00:44:37.711
The main way that Gojira cools itself
is through using blood flow. That's it.

883
00:44:37.794 --> 00:44:40.714
So it evolved to a sea creature in an
effort to regulate its body temperature...

884
00:44:40.797 --> 00:44:43.008
it couldn't cool as well when
it was the land creature it mutated into.

885
00:44:43.091 --> 00:44:44.092
is what you mean.

886
00:44:44.175 --> 00:44:46.678
Sounds like our only hope is to keep it
from regulating its temperature.

887
00:44:46.761 --> 00:44:49.097
Shut down its internal cooling system.

888
00:44:49.180 --> 00:44:50.849
If it's shut down.
Gojira will have no choice

889
00:44:50.932 --> 00:44:52.934
but to put its reactor into a scram state
to stay alive.

890
00:44:53.018 --> 00:44:55.645
This process of rapid cooling could freeze
its activity for a little while.

891
00:44:55.729 --> 00:44:58.273
but we have no idea if it will be enough
to kill it once and for all.

892
00:44:58.356 --> 00:44:59.774
What about the possibility
of orally administering

893
00:44:59.858 --> 00:45:01.902
a blood coagulation promoter
for this purpose.

894
00:45:01.985 --> 00:45:04.195
It's in an upright walking form.
Can it be done?

895
00:45:04.279 --> 00:45:06.448
We'll work out all the details
and create the best strategy.

896
00:45:06.531 --> 00:45:09.534
Just looking at it though.
maybe a pump truck could do the job.

897
00:45:09.618 --> 00:45:11.661
We. the Ministry of Health and METI

898
00:45:11.745 --> 00:45:13.788
can be in charge of gathering tools.
coagulant.

899
00:45:13.872 --> 00:45:15.457
and special vehicles
from all over the country.

900
00:45:15.540 --> 00:45:17.083
Take this to the Prime Minister
immediately.

901
00:45:17.167 --> 00:45:18.501
and call it the "Yaguchi Plan."

902
00:45:18.585 --> 00:45:20.170
Understood.

903
00:45:21.379 --> 00:45:23.715
However it's named. let's submit it.

904
00:45:25.258 --> 00:45:28.553
Gojira deserves to live! Gojira is a god!

905
00:45:28.637 --> 00:45:30.096
Gojira deserves to live!

906
00:45:30.180 --> 00:45:32.182
Gojira is a god!

907
00:45:59.542 --> 00:46:01.127
Thank you for your hard work.

908
00:46:01.211 --> 00:46:03.755
Oh. Thank you. as always.

909
00:46:03.838 --> 00:46:05.590
Thank you very much.

910
00:46:07.467 --> 00:46:09.928
Everyone. Let's take a break.

911
00:46:19.104 --> 00:46:22.732
I see everyone here doing all they can
without even being asked.

912
00:46:22.816 --> 00:46:24.776
Even though we tell them to go home
and rest.

913
00:46:24.859 --> 00:46:28.279
or see their families.
they choose not to go home.

914
00:46:28.363 --> 00:46:31.700
Or if they do. they return
with home-cooked meals for everyone.

915
00:46:32.784 --> 00:46:34.744
It's very encouraging sir.

916
00:46:34.828 --> 00:46:36.871
With the preparation
of the Gojira-related bills

917
00:46:36.955 --> 00:46:38.790
and Deputy Chairman Izumi's coordination.

918
00:46:38.873 --> 00:46:41.292
each ministry's working together
regardless of jurisdiction.

919
00:46:41.376 --> 00:46:44.295
A lot of outsiders from other departments
have also been working tirelessly

920
00:46:44.379 --> 00:46:46.464
because they volunteered to help us.

921
00:46:46.548 --> 00:46:48.758
You're right.

922
00:46:49.759 --> 00:46:52.095
This country has much to offer.

923
00:46:52.178 --> 00:46:53.638
That's how I feel.

924
00:46:53.722 --> 00:46:56.099
If I may ask a question though.

925
00:46:56.182 --> 00:46:58.852
How long ago did you last change
your shirt?

926
00:46:58.935 --> 00:46:59.978
Hmm?

927
00:47:00.061 --> 00:47:02.856
Honestly. it's making the room stink a bit.

928
00:47:04.983 --> 00:47:06.317
Really?

929
00:47:06.401 --> 00:47:09.279
If you're asking my opinion.
a shower would be best.

930
00:47:14.993 --> 00:47:16.494
Mr. Yaguchi.

931
00:47:16.578 --> 00:47:18.413
It appeared again
in Sagami Bay seconds ago.

932
00:47:18.496 --> 00:47:20.040
It's making its way to Kamakura.

933
00:47:36.473 --> 00:47:38.349
<i>Activate J-Alert.</i>

934
00:47:38.433 --> 00:47:40.894
<i>Transmit a warning of Gojira's arrival
at the shore.</i>

935
00:47:40.977 --> 00:47:44.355
<i>Prepare for transmission
of the primary alert over Em-Net.</i>

936
00:47:44.439 --> 00:47:49.277
<i>This is Kamakura Disaster Prevention.</i>

937
00:47:49.360 --> 00:47:53.531
<i>This is an evacuation
issued by the government.</i>

938
00:47:53.698 --> 00:47:59.996
<i>A Giant Unidentified Life-Form
has come ashore.</i>

939
00:48:00.080 --> 00:48:05.251
<i>An emergency evacuation order
has been issued.</i>

940
00:48:05.335 --> 00:48:11.132
<i>All citizens.
follow the instructions of the police.</i>

941
00:48:12.133 --> 00:48:14.010
The Prime Minister.

942
00:48:47.836 --> 00:48:51.131
<i>The target is passing through
Kamakura. and advancing toward Kamariya.</i>

943
00:48:51.214 --> 00:48:54.425
Wait. It's gotten a lot larger
since the first landing.

944
00:48:54.509 --> 00:48:56.678
Yeah. Beyond what we had theorized.

945
00:48:56.761 --> 00:48:58.805
Even its face and body are different. too.

946
00:48:58.888 --> 00:49:01.391
Yes. It looks to be nearly
double the size.

947
00:49:02.475 --> 00:49:03.685
Gojira has evolved.

948
00:49:03.768 --> 00:49:05.103
This would be his fourth form.

949
00:49:09.607 --> 00:49:11.985
It'll leave a trail of destruction
in its wake.

950
00:49:21.786 --> 00:49:23.788
<i>Residents outside the affected area.</i>

951
00:49:23.872 --> 00:49:25.582
<i>take refuge indoors!</i>

952
00:49:26.666 --> 00:49:29.544
<i>Going out without permission
is prohibited by law!</i>

953
00:49:29.627 --> 00:49:35.133
<i>You are in a designated evacuation zone!</i>

954
00:49:35.216 --> 00:49:37.468
<i>Attention. citizens!</i>

955
00:49:54.277 --> 00:49:56.279
<i>There's a high probability
that Gojira will reach Tokyo</i>

956
00:49:56.362 --> 00:49:57.488
<i>within three hours.</i>

957
00:49:57.572 --> 00:49:59.866
Why's it coming over here again?

958
00:50:22.388 --> 00:50:24.891
As stated in the handout here.
a direct assault on its body

959
00:50:24.974 --> 00:50:28.144
runs the risk of releasing radioactive
material into the environment.

960
00:50:28.228 --> 00:50:30.813
But we can't allow the capital
to be overrun again.

961
00:50:30.897 --> 00:50:33.900
so we think the top priority
should be preventing its attack.

962
00:50:33.983 --> 00:50:36.861
Radioactive material is the creature's
primary energy source.

963
00:50:36.945 --> 00:50:39.989
Just imagine if it attacked
one of our nuclear facilities.

964
00:50:40.073 --> 00:50:42.158
That would be a bigger disaster.

965
00:50:42.242 --> 00:50:45.620
Prime Minister. we have to strike.

966
00:50:45.703 --> 00:50:47.163
And right away.

967
00:50:47.247 --> 00:50:49.916
Prime Minister. we want to avoid
a situation where we're seen as weak

968
00:50:49.999 --> 00:50:51.542
or timid by the rest of the world.

969
00:50:51.626 --> 00:50:54.045
What of the Yaguchi Plan.
what's the current status?

970
00:50:54.128 --> 00:50:56.297
Unfortunately.
it's not ready to be put into action.

971
00:50:56.381 --> 00:51:00.260
Just give the order. and the SDF will do
its job. even in the urban areas.

972
00:51:00.343 --> 00:51:02.720
The declared state of emergency
is still in effect.

973
00:51:02.804 --> 00:51:04.806
The Prime Minister can order the attack.

974
00:51:04.889 --> 00:51:10.103
and that attack has to be decided
by the Prime Minister.

975
00:51:10.186 --> 00:51:11.771
Your call.

976
00:51:11.854 --> 00:51:13.731
I understand.

977
00:51:14.816 --> 00:51:15.858
I authorize it.

978
00:51:16.943 --> 00:51:18.486
Yes. Prime Minister.

979
00:51:18.569 --> 00:51:19.612
Contact command.

980
00:51:19.696 --> 00:51:20.697
Yes.

981
00:51:20.780 --> 00:51:23.157
The Prime Minister has ordered
the implementation of a new operation.

982
00:51:23.241 --> 00:51:25.451
We have unlimited weapon use.
is that clear?

983
00:51:25.535 --> 00:51:28.496
The Minister of Defense has told us
to do whatever it takes.

984
00:51:28.579 --> 00:51:31.165
We need to get rid of Gojira
before it reaches Tokyo.

985
00:51:31.249 --> 00:51:33.501
If it lands on Kanagawa.
we'll go with Operation B.

986
00:51:33.584 --> 00:51:35.670
Good. Activate B-2 with Kawasaki

987
00:51:35.753 --> 00:51:38.089
as the primary battleground
for the extermination.

988
00:51:38.172 --> 00:51:42.218
Roger that. The Tama River's the absolute
defense line in the case of B-2.

989
00:51:42.302 --> 00:51:43.678
Operation Taba's a go.

990
00:51:54.439 --> 00:51:57.066
<i>Attacker formation
will report five miles west.</i>

991
00:51:57.150 --> 00:51:59.819
<i>PO304. taking off from Tachikawa: 15:36.</i>

992
00:52:00.903 --> 00:52:02.363
<i>Tank and artillery battalions</i>

993
00:52:02.447 --> 00:52:04.032
<i>being deployed at Maruko Bridge.</i>

994
00:52:04.073 --> 00:52:05.825
<i>Roger. Prepare to fire.</i>

995
00:52:06.826 --> 00:52:08.828
This has to succeed.

996
00:52:08.911 --> 00:52:10.830
<i>Eight minutes until
expected time of encounter.</i>

997
00:52:10.913 --> 00:52:12.915
So we're really engaging in live fire?

998
00:52:12.999 --> 00:52:15.293
Relax. Do what you were trained to do.

999
00:52:15.376 --> 00:52:18.046
The target has radioactive material
in its body.

1000
00:52:18.129 --> 00:52:21.341
Therefore. we'll only pinpoint our attacks
on the head and legs.

1001
00:52:21.424 --> 00:52:23.718
I want all units to be aware of this.

1002
00:52:23.801 --> 00:52:27.055
Target approaching. Three minutes
until expected time of encounter.

1003
00:52:27.138 --> 00:52:30.600
1st to 4th anti-helicopter platoons.
arriving shortly.</i>

1004
00:52:33.811 --> 00:52:36.189
<i>CO1. this is CP. Over.</i>

1005
00:52:36.314 --> 00:52:38.191
<i>CP. CO1. Over.</i>

1006
00:52:38.274 --> 00:52:39.692
<i>CO1. CP.</i>

1007
00:52:39.776 --> 00:52:43.946
<i>PO1 in flight over Musashi-Kosugi Station.
holding at BP1.</i>

1008
00:52:44.030 --> 00:52:46.366
<i>PO2 to PO4 behind the towers.</i>

1009
00:52:46.449 --> 00:52:49.243
<i>Standby at holding area two. Over.</i>

1010
00:52:49.327 --> 00:52:51.412
<i>CP. CO1. BP approaching.</i>

1011
00:52:51.496 --> 00:52:53.915
<i>Target Distance. 1.200 meters. Over.</i>

1012
00:52:53.998 --> 00:52:56.334
<i>Roger that. Maintain positions. Over.</i>

1013
00:52:56.417 --> 00:52:59.170
Preparation for helicopter
reconnaissance. completed.

1014
00:52:59.253 --> 00:53:01.672
Total area evacuation is also completed.

1015
00:53:01.756 --> 00:53:05.635
Koriyama. are you entirely sure
there are no stragglers?

1016
00:53:05.718 --> 00:53:08.554
We just have to believe the reports
from the field.

1017
00:53:08.638 --> 00:53:10.765
The target is still advancing.

1018
00:53:10.848 --> 00:53:13.935
Prime Minister.
please authorize the use of weapons.

1019
00:53:14.018 --> 00:53:17.397
Weapons are authorized... from here on.

1020
00:53:17.480 --> 00:53:19.732
We've confirmed
the Prime Minister's order.

1021
00:53:19.816 --> 00:53:22.110
We can commence firing. Authorize it.

1022
00:53:22.193 --> 00:53:24.195
Taba Operation Phase One commence.

1023
00:53:24.278 --> 00:53:25.822
We are all clear to open fire now.

1024
00:53:25.905 --> 00:53:27.407
We are clear to fire. Over.

1025
00:53:27.490 --> 00:53:30.159
<i>CP. CO1. Roger. Firing.</i>

1026
00:53:30.243 --> 00:53:32.078
Ready. Fire.

1027
00:53:40.044 --> 00:53:42.713
Autocannon.
All rounds. direct hits. Ineffective.

1028
00:53:44.632 --> 00:53:46.342
Apache 30-millimeter ready.

1029
00:53:46.426 --> 00:53:47.760
Let's see what that does.

1030
00:53:56.227 --> 00:53:57.437
<i>Ninja ACP.</i>

1031
00:53:57.520 --> 00:53:59.981
<i>Third wave of reconnaissance in progress.
Report results.</i>

1032
00:54:00.064 --> 00:54:01.524
<i>3rd Squadron engaged.</i>

1033
00:54:01.607 --> 00:54:03.568
Target fine. Weapons had no effect.

1034
00:54:03.651 --> 00:54:06.821
16.000 rounds of machine-gun fire later...

1035
00:54:06.904 --> 00:54:09.240
and not even a single scratch.

1036
00:54:09.323 --> 00:54:10.950
Contact headquarters and the PM.

1037
00:54:11.033 --> 00:54:15.204
The Eastern Army Commander is requesting
permission to use guided missiles.

1038
00:54:16.372 --> 00:54:18.708
It's a dense area. but we have no choice.

1039
00:54:18.791 --> 00:54:20.543
I strongly urge you to grant permission.

1040
00:54:20.626 --> 00:54:23.045
Unlimited weapon use...

1041
00:54:23.129 --> 00:54:25.965
Is officially authorized.

1042
00:54:26.048 --> 00:54:27.216
Do what you must.

1043
00:54:27.300 --> 00:54:29.177
<i>CO1. CP.</i>

1044
00:54:29.260 --> 00:54:30.720
<i>Switch assault to guided missiles.</i>

1045
00:54:30.803 --> 00:54:33.222
<i>As soon as preparations are complete.
fire them all! Over.</i>

1046
00:54:33.306 --> 00:54:34.432
<i>Roger that.</i>

1047
00:54:34.515 --> 00:54:36.851
<i>PO1 to PO4. fire all guided missiles!</i>

1048
00:54:36.934 --> 00:54:38.603
<i>Giant creature straight ahead.</i>

1049
00:54:38.686 --> 00:54:40.396
<i>700.</i>

1050
00:54:40.480 --> 00:54:42.607
<i>Prepare to fire. Fire!</i>

1051
00:54:48.529 --> 00:54:50.531
<i>TOW. Hellfire. Fire all rounds!</i>

1052
00:55:03.419 --> 00:55:05.713
"All direct hits yet no visible
or clear damage to the creature."

1053
00:55:05.796 --> 00:55:07.173
End of the report.

1054
00:55:07.256 --> 00:55:09.008
The missiles aren't even hurting it.

1055
00:55:09.091 --> 00:55:10.343
What the hell is that?!

1056
00:55:10.426 --> 00:55:13.221
The outer shell is harder to pierce
than we had expected.

1057
00:55:13.304 --> 00:55:15.473
We'll shift the operation to Phase Two.

1058
00:55:15.556 --> 00:55:16.641
Tiger 1. CP.

1059
00:55:16.724 --> 00:55:18.518
Taba Operation Phase Two commence.

1060
00:55:18.601 --> 00:55:19.977
You are clear to fire.

1061
00:55:20.061 --> 00:55:22.104
I repeat. You are clear to fire. Over.</i>

1062
00:55:22.188 --> 00:55:23.231
<i>Roger that. Tiger.</i>

1063
00:55:23.314 --> 00:55:26.609
<i>This is Tiger 1.
Commence fire. Commence fire.</i>

1064
00:55:26.692 --> 00:55:28.402
<i>Type 10 tanks. Target ahead.
Aim for its legs.</i>

1065
00:55:28.486 --> 00:55:30.655
<i>Anti-tank concentrated barrage.
Give orders!</i>

1066
00:55:30.738 --> 00:55:33.533
<i>All vehicles. Loaded. Ready to fire.</i>

1067
00:55:34.659 --> 00:55:36.661
<i>Distance good. Fire!</i>

1068
00:55:40.706 --> 00:55:42.416
Direct hit. Continue to fire!

1069
00:55:48.548 --> 00:55:50.758
The target. its speed appears
to have decreased!

1070
00:55:50.841 --> 00:55:52.176
Good. Let's keep pushing then.

1071
00:55:52.260 --> 00:55:53.719
Layer on some artillery fire.

1072
00:55:56.639 --> 00:56:00.226
Time on target. ten. eight. seven.</i>

1073
00:56:00.309 --> 00:56:04.021
<i>six. five. four. three...</i>

1074
00:56:04.105 --> 00:56:06.190
<i>Impact now.</i>

1075
00:56:07.984 --> 00:56:09.443
All shells hit the target!

1076
00:56:09.527 --> 00:56:11.028
Fusillade. Fire!

1077
00:56:35.344 --> 00:56:38.306
Target has crossed the levee
and is now entering the Tama River!

1078
00:56:38.389 --> 00:56:40.850
Inform Gotemba and Special Forces.
Commence attack.

1079
00:56:51.694 --> 00:56:53.487
The target has halted!

1080
00:56:53.571 --> 00:56:55.406
It's time to shift to Phase Three now.

1081
00:56:55.489 --> 00:56:57.617
Start the aerial assault right away.

1082
00:56:57.700 --> 00:56:59.160
<i>Type 10 tanks. This is 10.</i>

1083
00:56:59.243 --> 00:57:00.286
<i>Move to Phase Three.</i>

1084
00:57:00.369 --> 00:57:01.787
<i>All vehicles to new positions!</i>

1085
00:57:01.871 --> 00:57:03.831
<i>I repeat. all vehicles to new positions!</i>

1086
00:57:27.396 --> 00:57:29.148
<i>The target is changing course
to northwest.</i>

1087
00:57:29.231 --> 00:57:31.776
<i>I repeat. changing course to northwest!</i>

1088
00:57:31.859 --> 00:57:33.194
Why's it turning away?

1089
00:57:33.277 --> 00:57:34.779
Does that mean the airstrike's working?

1090
00:57:34.862 --> 00:57:36.864
JDAM second wave incoming.

1091
00:57:36.947 --> 00:57:38.866
Good. this will certainly finish it.

1092
00:57:49.293 --> 00:57:50.544
We did it.

1093
00:57:53.798 --> 00:57:54.924
All vehicles evacuate!

1094
00:58:27.331 --> 00:58:29.208
Evacuate! Evacuate!

1095
00:58:29.291 --> 00:58:31.210
Evacuate!

1096
00:58:35.673 --> 00:58:38.300
<i>Target's crossed the Tama River
and is now entering Tokyo!</i>

1097
00:58:38.384 --> 00:58:39.593
<i>ACP. CO1.</i>

1098
00:58:39.677 --> 00:58:41.595
<i>All aircraft. all weapons.
out of munitions.</i>

1099
00:58:41.679 --> 00:58:43.597
<i>I repeat. all weapons. out of munitions.</i>

1100
00:58:43.681 --> 00:58:45.057
<i>Tiger 1. This is 40.</i>

1101
00:58:45.141 --> 00:58:47.143
<i>Visibility zero. Target unconfirmed.</i>

1102
00:58:47.226 --> 00:58:48.644
<i>CP. This is Tiger 1.</i>

1103
00:58:48.728 --> 00:58:50.312
<i>The 8th platoon is out of munitions.</i>

1104
00:58:50.396 --> 00:58:54.150
<i>Three tanks are severely damaged.
two are moderately damaged. Over.</i>

1105
00:59:00.114 --> 00:59:01.741
<i>Forward command post destroyed.</i>

1106
00:59:01.824 --> 00:59:03.492
<i>Taba Combat Group loses command.</i>

1107
00:59:03.576 --> 00:59:05.411
<i>Target's breached the defense line.</i>

1108
00:59:05.494 --> 00:59:08.122
<i>Defensive position has collapsed.
Operation cannot continue.</i>

1109
00:59:10.166 --> 00:59:13.043
Joint Staff Vice Chief.

1110
00:59:13.127 --> 00:59:15.671
the creature's still within
artillery range.

1111
00:59:15.755 --> 00:59:17.173
We need to continue the offense.

1112
00:59:17.256 --> 00:59:21.093
We can't. We haven't received word
on the evacuation in Ota and Setagaya.

1113
00:59:21.177 --> 00:59:22.720
Ah! We're sorry.

1114
00:59:22.803 --> 00:59:24.388
We're afraid this is all we can do.

1115
00:59:24.472 --> 00:59:26.098
Understood.

1116
00:59:27.600 --> 00:59:29.393
Operation suspended.

1117
00:59:29.477 --> 00:59:32.480
We couldn't hold it back.
It's disappointing.

1118
00:59:32.563 --> 00:59:33.939
Don't let it discourage you.

1119
00:59:34.023 --> 00:59:35.983
Our job is to protect the people first.

1120
00:59:36.066 --> 00:59:37.902
Attacking isn't the only way.

1121
00:59:37.985 --> 00:59:40.404
Speed up the evacuations.

1122
00:59:40.488 --> 00:59:41.947
Operation Taba has failed.

1123
00:59:42.031 --> 00:59:43.741
Gojira's unscathed. It's relocating again.

1124
00:59:43.824 --> 00:59:46.410
The Self-Defense Forces' full power
was futile.

1125
00:59:46.494 --> 00:59:49.246
Its ability to defend itself
exceeded our calculations.

1126
00:59:49.330 --> 00:59:51.081
If we could just defeat it
using physical weapons.

1127
00:59:51.165 --> 00:59:52.833
we wouldn't be here struggling so much.

1128
00:59:52.917 --> 00:59:55.544
Is it really a perfect creature
beyond human understanding?

1129
01:00:03.219 --> 01:00:05.721
<i>Target's moving from Setagaya Ward
to Meguro Ward.</i>

1130
01:00:05.805 --> 01:00:08.474
Prime Minister.
let's petition the U.S. troops in Japan

1131
01:00:08.557 --> 01:00:10.726
to cooperate
in the creature's extermination.

1132
01:00:10.810 --> 01:00:12.520
Prime Minister. from the U.S. Ambassador.

1133
01:00:12.603 --> 01:00:15.022
U.S. Air Force bombers have already
taken off from Guam.

1134
01:00:15.105 --> 01:00:16.190
They're on their way now.

1135
01:00:20.319 --> 01:00:22.488
Submit a formal cooperation request
to the U.S. quickly.

1136
01:00:22.571 --> 01:00:24.615
I'll find the ambassador
at Yokota and get authorization.

1137
01:00:24.698 --> 01:00:26.408
I suggest holding
an emergency news conference

1138
01:00:26.492 --> 01:00:28.160
regarding the U.S. forces in Japan.

1139
01:00:28.244 --> 01:00:30.996
<i>We've requested that
the U.S. military assist us.</i>

1140
01:00:31.080 --> 01:00:33.040
<i>They'll cooperate
in the extermination of Gojira</i>

1141
01:00:33.123 --> 01:00:35.125
<i>under the Japan-U.S Security Treaty.</i>

1142
01:00:51.225 --> 01:00:54.228
This is the bombing zone
proposed by the U.S.

1143
01:00:54.311 --> 01:00:55.938
The area will be this wide?

1144
01:00:56.021 --> 01:00:58.023
This is crazy.
This is even worse than Gojira.

1145
01:00:58.107 --> 01:00:59.692
We can't transport them all.

1146
01:00:59.775 --> 01:01:02.111
Evacuate citizens
to underground structures.

1147
01:01:02.194 --> 01:01:05.281
<i>The U.S. military will begin launching
their attack on Gojira!</i>

1148
01:01:05.364 --> 01:01:06.907
<i>For your safety. go underground!</i>

1149
01:01:06.991 --> 01:01:09.243
<i>Evacuate to subways and underground malls!</i>

1150
01:01:09.326 --> 01:01:11.203
Calm down! Yes!

1151
01:01:19.253 --> 01:01:20.421
Don't push!

1152
01:01:45.946 --> 01:01:49.533
This location is located
directly in Gojira's path.

1153
01:01:49.617 --> 01:01:52.244
Our Self-Defense Forces
couldn't eradicate it.

1154
01:01:52.328 --> 01:01:54.830
It's likely that the U.S. forces
will also fail.

1155
01:01:54.914 --> 01:01:56.457
What are you saying?

1156
01:01:56.540 --> 01:01:58.167
You really want us to evacuate?

1157
01:01:58.250 --> 01:01:59.460
Yes!

1158
01:01:59.543 --> 01:02:01.587
Ichigaya and Ariake are dangerous. too!

1159
01:02:01.670 --> 01:02:03.172
We have to leave as soon as we can.

1160
01:02:03.255 --> 01:02:06.216
We'll transfer the functions of
the Prime Minister's office to Tachikawa.

1161
01:02:06.300 --> 01:02:09.511
They're about to start their airstrike
at Tokyo in any minute.

1162
01:02:09.595 --> 01:02:11.430
My duty is to stay here.

1163
01:02:11.513 --> 01:02:13.724
We all have a duty
to keep track of this mission.

1164
01:02:13.807 --> 01:02:15.643
We can't abandon our citizens.

1165
01:02:15.726 --> 01:02:17.519
We can't run away in the face of danger!

1166
01:02:17.603 --> 01:02:19.313
Prime Minister.

1167
01:02:19.396 --> 01:02:21.815
As our leader. it's your duty to protect
the nation and its people.

1168
01:02:21.899 --> 01:02:25.319
even if that means abandoning Tokyo.
so I urge you to leave.

1169
01:02:25.402 --> 01:02:27.988
Fortunately.
the Tokyo government's still functioning.

1170
01:02:28.072 --> 01:02:32.117
So what we should do is leave
Governor Kozuka in command just for now.

1171
01:02:33.661 --> 01:02:35.329
Very well.

1172
01:02:35.412 --> 01:02:37.456
We'll prepare two helicopters
from Kisarazu.

1173
01:02:37.539 --> 01:02:39.750
Sir. I'll travel with my team by car.

1174
01:02:39.833 --> 01:02:42.336
All right then. Go ahead.

1175
01:02:42.419 --> 01:02:45.047
That is going to take some time.

1176
01:02:45.130 --> 01:02:48.008
The traffic will be horrendous.

1177
01:02:48.926 --> 01:02:50.344
We'll see you there.

1178
01:02:50.427 --> 01:02:53.222
Yes. I will make sure of it.

1179
01:02:53.305 --> 01:02:56.308
A mandatory evacuation order
has been issued

1180
01:02:56.392 --> 01:02:58.143
due to the approach of a giant creature!

1181
01:02:58.227 --> 01:03:00.396
Everyone please evacuate at once!

1182
01:03:00.479 --> 01:03:02.648
A mandatory evacuation order
has been issued

1183
01:03:02.731 --> 01:03:04.817
due to the approach of a giant creature!

1184
01:03:04.900 --> 01:03:06.110
Everyone please evacuate at once!

1185
01:03:06.193 --> 01:03:08.278
Go. go! Let's go! Come on!

1186
01:03:17.287 --> 01:03:19.081
Everywhere is gridlocked like this.

1187
01:03:19.164 --> 01:03:20.708
We're not going anywhere.

1188
01:03:20.791 --> 01:03:22.001
Looks like it.

1189
01:03:22.084 --> 01:03:23.585
The military will attack soon.

1190
01:03:23.669 --> 01:03:25.587
We need to get everyone underground.

1191
01:03:35.305 --> 01:03:37.266
So that's Gojira.

1192
01:03:37.349 --> 01:03:40.978
Deputy Chief. the U.S. airstrike is
starting earlier than originally planned.

1193
01:03:47.568 --> 01:03:49.737
The target sustained damage
from both of the MOP II bombs.

1194
01:03:49.820 --> 01:03:51.780
Bleeding confirmed. A successful strike.

1195
01:03:54.533 --> 01:03:55.868
Finally.

1196
01:03:55.951 --> 01:03:57.703
Way to go. U.S.A.

1197
01:04:06.211 --> 01:04:09.423
Prime Minister. the helicopters
will arrive any minute.

1198
01:04:22.895 --> 01:04:25.439
- Over here. everyone. down the stairs!
- Remain calm!

1199
01:04:25.522 --> 01:04:27.274
- Underground!
- What's that light?

1200
01:04:39.787 --> 01:04:42.456
The organ that controls heat on its back
has started glowing all of a sudden!

1201
01:04:42.539 --> 01:04:44.041
We have no further details!

1202
01:04:44.124 --> 01:04:46.126
What's it doing now?

1203
01:05:14.113 --> 01:05:15.280
I don't see anybody else.

1204
01:05:15.364 --> 01:05:16.824
Come on. let's get inside.

1205
01:05:30.754 --> 01:05:32.673
The name truly suits it.

1206
01:06:13.297 --> 01:06:14.715
<i>Taking off 18:35.</i>

1207
01:06:14.798 --> 01:06:16.049
<i>Transporting the Prime Minister
and eight others...</i>

1208
01:07:20.948 --> 01:07:23.825
<i>High levels of radiation
are to be expected.</i>

1209
01:07:23.909 --> 01:07:27.788
<i>All Tokyo residents are urged
to remain indoors for at least 49 hours...</i>

1210
01:07:27.871 --> 01:07:29.957
<i>Just how much radioactive material
did Gojira release on Tokyo?</i>

1211
01:07:30.040 --> 01:07:32.000
<i>The radiation exposure caused
by the giant unknown creature...</i>

1212
01:07:32.084 --> 01:07:33.669
<i>Don't rely on the government.</i>

1213
01:07:33.752 --> 01:07:35.128
<i>There's a confirmed hot spot over there.</i>

1214
01:07:35.212 --> 01:07:37.297
<i>The radiation levels in the air are high.</i>

1215
01:07:37.381 --> 01:07:39.549
<i>Should we distribute the stable
iodine tablets we have in stock.</i>

1216
01:07:39.633 --> 01:07:41.343
<i>or should we use them immediately?</i>

1217
01:07:41.426 --> 01:07:43.720
<i>Fire and Rescue Mobile Units. from
the 3rd and 9th Regional headquarters...</i>

1218
01:07:43.804 --> 01:07:45.138
<i>There's a risk of a secondary disaster.</i>

1219
01:07:45.222 --> 01:07:47.015
<i>...have been dispatched
for decontamination and rescue</i>

1220
01:07:47.099 --> 01:07:49.434
<i>within the Tokyo metropolitan area.</i>

1221
01:07:49.518 --> 01:07:52.688
<i>The safety of Prime Minister Okouchi.
Chief Cabinet Secretary Azuma.</i>

1222
01:07:52.771 --> 01:07:55.148
<i>and the five other people scheduled
to become acting Prime Ministers</i>

1223
01:07:55.232 --> 01:07:56.692
<i>are all unknown.</i>

1224
01:07:56.775 --> 01:07:59.236
<i>The Metropolitan Police Department.
the MLIT. and the MIC...</i>

1225
01:07:59.319 --> 01:08:01.238
<i>We need to restore
the telephone lines ASAP.</i>

1226
01:08:01.321 --> 01:08:03.031
<i>Combine our dedicated lines.
public lines and private lines.</i>

1227
01:08:03.115 --> 01:08:05.951
<i>There's no prospect of any infrastructure
in the affected areas being restored.</i>

1228
01:08:06.034 --> 01:08:08.287
<i>Going forward we will need
to consider moving the capital</i>

1229
01:08:08.370 --> 01:08:12.249
<i>to Saitama New Urban Center.
Sapporo. Fukuoka...</i>

1230
01:08:12.332 --> 01:08:14.459
<i>We're unable to contact a significant
number of embassies in Japan...</i>

1231
01:08:14.543 --> 01:08:16.003
<i>A huge number of evacuees...</i>

1232
01:08:16.086 --> 01:08:18.630
<i>Foreigners living in Japan are being
advised by their home countries</i>

1233
01:08:18.714 --> 01:08:20.424
<i>to leave Japan and return home
on chartered flights...</i>

1234
01:08:20.507 --> 01:08:23.802
<i>In order to avoid a political vacuum.
several cabinet ministers</i>

1235
01:08:23.885 --> 01:08:26.888
<i>who have been contacted are currently
in discussions with ruling party officials</i>

1236
01:08:26.972 --> 01:08:28.974
<i>to select an acting Prime Minister.</i>

1237
01:08:29.057 --> 01:08:30.976
<i>With the Prime Minister's
residence in danger.</i>

1238
01:08:31.059 --> 01:08:33.270
<i>federal headquarters
have officially relocated</i>

1239
01:08:33.353 --> 01:08:36.356
<i>to the Tachikawa-wide Area
Disaster Prevention Base.</i>

1240
01:08:36.440 --> 01:08:39.693
<i>which was established as a temporary base
in the event of an emergency.</i>

1241
01:08:39.776 --> 01:08:41.695
<i>This is a notice to all visitors</i>

1242
01:08:41.778 --> 01:08:45.907
<i>of the Tachikawa Disaster Prevention
Joint Government Building.</i>

1243
01:08:45.991 --> 01:08:47.826
- Deputy Chief Yaguchi.
- I'll call you later.

1244
01:08:47.909 --> 01:08:49.202
Mr. Izumi.

1245
01:08:49.286 --> 01:08:50.871
Well. I'm glad you're safe.

1246
01:08:50.954 --> 01:08:52.914
It was a good thing
that I visited home on Friday.

1247
01:08:52.998 --> 01:08:55.125
You should think of visiting
your hometown. too.

1248
01:08:55.208 --> 01:08:57.544
Hey. You look like you're injured.
You okay?

1249
01:08:57.627 --> 01:09:00.297
I'm sorry. First aid supplies
are out of stock everywhere.

1250
01:09:00.380 --> 01:09:02.174
I'm fine. It's nothing serious.

1251
01:09:03.175 --> 01:09:04.676
Fire department personnel

1252
01:09:04.760 --> 01:09:06.636
should follow
the Tokyo Metropolitan Government.

1253
01:09:06.720 --> 01:09:08.347
Let the police
take care of the homeless refugees.

1254
01:09:08.430 --> 01:09:09.681
They won't die
if you leave them overnight!

1255
01:09:09.765 --> 01:09:11.683
The affected population
is estimated to be three million.

1256
01:09:11.767 --> 01:09:13.477
We need to get a jump on the press.

1257
01:09:14.478 --> 01:09:16.563
All right. I need to hear
the latest intel.

1258
01:09:16.646 --> 01:09:17.939
What's the situation?

1259
01:09:18.023 --> 01:09:19.107
All we can say is it's still inactive.

1260
01:09:19.191 --> 01:09:21.318
We're not sure why it suddenly stopped.
but it's near Tokyo Station.

1261
01:09:21.401 --> 01:09:22.903
Current radiation levels?

1262
01:09:22.986 --> 01:09:24.905
The Nuclear Regulation Authority
is still taking readings.

1263
01:09:24.988 --> 01:09:27.449
They're busy surveying
the whole metro area.

1264
01:09:27.491 --> 01:09:30.077
Gojira's still releasing trace amounts
of radioactive material

1265
01:09:30.160 --> 01:09:32.746
from its mouth. however.
this level won't be an issue.

1266
01:09:32.829 --> 01:09:35.207
Gojira's plume has drifted out to sea.

1267
01:09:35.290 --> 01:09:37.542
and yet. we're looking at a wide area
of contamination.

1268
01:09:37.626 --> 01:09:40.379
The three wards in Tokyo that were hit
directly may be uninhabitable.

1269
01:09:40.462 --> 01:09:42.381
Decontamination could be an issue.

1270
01:09:42.464 --> 01:09:44.925
The situation is extremely serious.
life-or-death.

1271
01:09:45.008 --> 01:09:48.303
But we don't have nearly enough manpower
or supplies or even legal infrastructure.

1272
01:09:48.387 --> 01:09:49.763
There was nothing we could do.

1273
01:09:49.846 --> 01:09:52.724
The Prime Minister. Minister Hanamori.
the Chief Cabinet Secretary...

1274
01:09:52.808 --> 01:09:54.601
I'm afraid all of them are dead.

1275
01:09:54.684 --> 01:09:56.520
Don't rely on those who aren't here!

1276
01:09:56.603 --> 01:09:59.272
Those who remain now.
we just need to do what we can!

1277
01:09:59.356 --> 01:10:01.233
Yaguchi.

1278
01:10:01.316 --> 01:10:04.194
<i>- I regret to report that
their deaths have now been confirmed.</i>
- You need to calm yourself down.

1279
01:10:04.277 --> 01:10:07.072
<i>Prime Minister Okouchi
and 11 other Cabinet members.</i>

1280
01:10:07.155 --> 01:10:09.616
<i>including Foreign Affairs
Minister Kunihira.</i>

1281
01:10:09.699 --> 01:10:12.452
<i>Minister of Health.
Labor and Welfare Iwata.</i>

1282
01:10:12.536 --> 01:10:15.330
- Good.
<i>- and Chief Cabinet Secretary Azuma
were among them.</i>

1283
01:10:15.414 --> 01:10:19.000
<i>Surviving cabinet ministers are in
discussions with ruling party officials</i>

1284
01:10:19.084 --> 01:10:21.211
<i>to select an acting Prime Minister
in an effort...</i>

1285
01:10:21.294 --> 01:10:23.171
I'm sorry.

1286
01:10:23.255 --> 01:10:25.715
<i>And there is still a risk
of a secondary disaster.</i>

1287
01:10:25.799 --> 01:10:27.843
So who's the acting Prime Minister
right now?

1288
01:10:27.926 --> 01:10:30.470
<i>The ruling party has reached a decision.</i>

1289
01:10:30.554 --> 01:10:35.142
<i>The Minister of Agriculture. Forestry
and Fisheries. Yusuke Satomi.</i>

1290
01:10:35.225 --> 01:10:37.102
<i>has been appointed acting Prime Minister.</i>

1291
01:10:37.185 --> 01:10:40.730
<i>This emergency measure is to ensure
the government continues to function</i>

1292
01:10:40.814 --> 01:10:43.275
<i>and to avoid a political vacuum.</i>

1293
01:10:43.358 --> 01:10:46.403
Regardless. he's not only
received the Prime Minister's Award.

1294
01:10:46.486 --> 01:10:49.406
he also has the clear advantage
of factional seniority.

1295
01:10:49.489 --> 01:10:52.409
Look where he is now...
he's the Prime Minister.

1296
01:10:52.492 --> 01:10:55.370
I hear it was the Secretary General
and the rest of the ministers

1297
01:10:55.454 --> 01:10:56.621
who forced it on him.

1298
01:10:56.705 --> 01:10:57.789
Think of it this way.

1299
01:10:57.873 --> 01:11:00.292
In times like these.
no one wants to take responsibility.

1300
01:11:00.375 --> 01:11:04.004
From Sasebo. there's some disturbing
activity off the coast of Tsushima.

1301
01:11:04.087 --> 01:11:07.507
Very well.
I suppose we'll just have to wait and see.

1302
01:11:07.591 --> 01:11:10.218
Can the Minister of Foreign Affair
take action?

1303
01:11:10.302 --> 01:11:13.013
We're working to restore it
as we speak. It'll be soon.

1304
01:11:13.096 --> 01:11:14.639
I see.

1305
01:11:14.723 --> 01:11:17.517
Then try to avoid
any unforeseen circumstances.

1306
01:11:17.601 --> 01:11:21.188
Yes. I'll be sure to convey that
to the ambassador.

1307
01:11:28.320 --> 01:11:31.740
Ah. My noodles got soggy.

1308
01:11:34.075 --> 01:11:37.579
Turns out being Prime Minister
is a lot harder than I thought.

1309
01:11:38.371 --> 01:11:41.416
Yeah. he's a difficult man to read.

1310
01:11:41.500 --> 01:11:45.003
Whoever the Prime Minister is.
it's our duty to support the country.

1311
01:11:45.086 --> 01:11:47.881
We need to draft
the emergency legislation.

1312
01:11:47.964 --> 01:11:50.634
However. 30 kilometers away.
Gojira's currently resting.

1313
01:11:50.717 --> 01:11:52.093
You're not worried?

1314
01:11:52.177 --> 01:11:55.180
No need to worry about a political vacuum
if we're attacked over here.

1315
01:11:55.263 --> 01:11:57.474
If I've learned anything.
it's that one of Japan's strengths

1316
01:11:57.557 --> 01:11:59.476
is deciding its next leader quickly.

1317
01:11:59.559 --> 01:12:00.685
Does that mean you're next?

1318
01:12:00.769 --> 01:12:02.979
No way.

1319
01:12:05.273 --> 01:12:06.942
Perhaps in ten years though.

1320
01:12:07.025 --> 01:12:08.860
Well. if Japan's still around
in ten years.

1321
01:12:08.944 --> 01:12:10.445
you should definitely run for office.

1322
01:12:10.529 --> 01:12:11.696
You'll get my vote.

1323
01:12:11.780 --> 01:12:13.949
I'll take Secretary General in exchange.

1324
01:12:17.577 --> 01:12:21.831
I heard that Akasaka was safe since
he was at Yokota before it all went down.

1325
01:12:21.915 --> 01:12:25.710
A politician needs strategy.
and good luck as well.

1326
01:12:25.794 --> 01:12:29.047
Now he's acting Chief Cabinet Secretary.
just look at him.

1327
01:12:29.130 --> 01:12:31.091
Why can't you be more like that.

1328
01:12:31.174 --> 01:12:32.509
Play the game.

1329
01:12:34.719 --> 01:12:37.097
You're Minister for Special Missions
and Deputy Director.

1330
01:12:37.180 --> 01:12:38.974
That's unique.

1331
01:12:39.057 --> 01:12:41.685
You're the de facto executive officer now.

1332
01:12:41.768 --> 01:12:44.229
It sounds nice. but I'll be the one
to take the fall if we fail.

1333
01:12:44.312 --> 01:12:46.648
That's Akasaka's clever strategy.

1334
01:12:47.566 --> 01:12:49.985
You'll be selected as the new aide
to the Prime Minister.

1335
01:12:50.068 --> 01:12:52.070
That's the position you want. isn't it?

1336
01:12:52.153 --> 01:12:54.364
What's wrong with advancing your career?

1337
01:12:55.031 --> 01:12:57.993
Why'd you become a politician.
if you're not into that?

1338
01:12:58.076 --> 01:12:59.703
'Cause you always know
who your friends are.

1339
01:12:59.786 --> 01:13:01.496
It's simple. That's why I like it.

1340
01:13:01.580 --> 01:13:04.541
Deputy Director.
Bureau members have arrived.

1341
01:13:08.587 --> 01:13:10.964
More than half of our team survived.

1342
01:13:11.047 --> 01:13:13.883
I'm grateful that you're all here
in light of this recent tragedy.

1343
01:13:13.967 --> 01:13:15.385
Thank you.

1344
01:13:16.511 --> 01:13:19.514
Our hearts are heavy for those who.
unfortunately. didn't make it.

1345
01:13:20.557 --> 01:13:23.560
We have to do our best on behalf of them.

1346
01:13:23.643 --> 01:13:25.645
And we must keep moving forward.

1347
01:13:25.729 --> 01:13:27.856
The sadness of losing loved ones
and colleagues.

1348
01:13:27.939 --> 01:13:30.692
I'm sorry to say. never truly goes away.

1349
01:13:30.775 --> 01:13:32.986
However. we can all prevail.

1350
01:13:34.279 --> 01:13:36.781
So. for the sake of the people.

1351
01:13:36.906 --> 01:13:40.869
I ask you to pour your heart and souls
into finishing our work here.

1352
01:13:41.578 --> 01:13:43.079
I beg you.

1353
01:13:50.920 --> 01:13:52.213
Let's all get back to work.

1354
01:14:04.309 --> 01:14:05.560
- Chief Mori.
- Yes.

1355
01:14:05.644 --> 01:14:07.228
What's the update on the freezing plan?

1356
01:14:07.312 --> 01:14:09.981
Due to a lack of data.
private companies are working separately

1357
01:14:10.065 --> 01:14:13.068
to create around 24 different
prototypes of blood clotting promoters

1358
01:14:13.151 --> 01:14:15.862
using silica. thrombin and other agents.

1359
01:14:15.945 --> 01:14:17.739
One of these ought to work on Gojira.

1360
01:14:17.822 --> 01:14:18.823
How can we verify that?

1361
01:14:18.948 --> 01:14:20.867
We've already asked the GSDF to collect
biological cells

1362
01:14:20.950 --> 01:14:22.869
and we'll use those samples
to narrow it down.

1363
01:14:27.207 --> 01:14:28.792
Roger that.

1364
01:14:28.875 --> 01:14:30.418
The samples were collected. sir.

1365
01:14:31.044 --> 01:14:33.672
Then we'll go ahead and send them
to BSL-4 labs in Tsukuba immediately.

1366
01:14:33.755 --> 01:14:34.881
Understood.

1367
01:14:34.964 --> 01:14:37.425
Send all of the remaining samples
to a P3-level facility.

1368
01:14:37.509 --> 01:14:38.927
whether public or private.

1369
01:14:39.010 --> 01:14:41.721
However. these are classified substances.
so that's a bad idea.

1370
01:14:41.805 --> 01:14:44.432
It's all right. We need as much info
on Gojira as we can get.

1371
01:14:46.059 --> 01:14:48.186
No change to the radiation levels
in the air.

1372
01:14:48.269 --> 01:14:50.647
It's stable at around 0.8 to 1 sievert.

1373
01:14:50.730 --> 01:14:52.023
He's a quiet sleeper.

1374
01:14:52.107 --> 01:14:54.275
Well. then. that means
it's storing it all up in its stomach.

1375
01:14:55.777 --> 01:14:57.112
Shift change. Fall back.

1376
01:14:59.864 --> 01:15:01.533
This is Yaguchi.

1377
01:15:01.616 --> 01:15:03.368
We're arriving in five.

1378
01:15:03.451 --> 01:15:06.037
Can you secure us a meeting
with the acting Prime Minister?

1379
01:15:06.121 --> 01:15:09.624
To be clear. you'd like to provide us with
knowledge from the United States

1380
01:15:09.708 --> 01:15:11.459
to assist in our fight?

1381
01:15:57.380 --> 01:16:00.133
A U.S.-Japan Gojira research coalition?

1382
01:16:00.216 --> 01:16:01.718
It'll be all right.

1383
01:16:01.801 --> 01:16:03.052
The more knowledge. the better.

1384
01:16:03.136 --> 01:16:05.305
Let's clear some space for them.

1385
01:16:09.100 --> 01:16:13.229
Footage from the GSDF's latest unmanned
reconnaissance aircraft system.

1386
01:16:17.025 --> 01:16:18.735
After the attack. it immediately froze.

1387
01:16:18.818 --> 01:16:20.862
It seems Gojira froze immediately
after the attack. like the simulation.

1388
01:16:20.945 --> 01:16:22.363
Same as the D2 simulation.

1389
01:16:28.203 --> 01:16:31.331
So It's safe to assume
that all approaching flying objects

1390
01:16:31.414 --> 01:16:33.124
will be instinctively intercepted.

1391
01:16:36.377 --> 01:16:38.129
<i>Squad 2. this is CV1.</i>

1392
01:16:38.213 --> 01:16:39.923
<i>Five minutes from point zero.</i>

1393
01:16:40.006 --> 01:16:41.633
<i>Ten minutes remaining. Over.</i>

1394
01:16:41.716 --> 01:16:43.843
CV1. Squad 2. Roger that.

1395
01:16:51.851 --> 01:16:54.813
We've cross-referenced field data
with the data from Tsukuba.

1396
01:16:54.896 --> 01:16:58.191
and it's possible that Gojira
will reproduce asexually.

1397
01:16:59.651 --> 01:17:03.530
We anticipate the number of individuals
to grow exponentially around the world.

1398
01:17:03.613 --> 01:17:07.075
From an evolutionary view.
they could reduce in size

1399
01:17:07.158 --> 01:17:10.537
and then sprout wings and spread globally.

1400
01:17:27.220 --> 01:17:30.890
In Washington. the Secretary of Defense
is arguing that...

1401
01:17:30.974 --> 01:17:35.395
He wants to dispose of Godzilla
with a thermonuclear weapon.

1402
01:17:35.478 --> 01:17:37.313
And what's the take from the White House?

1403
01:17:37.397 --> 01:17:40.108
A report shown to the President
said there's a 13% chance

1404
01:17:40.191 --> 01:17:42.694
that Godzilla will land on the West Coast.

1405
01:17:42.777 --> 01:17:45.738
Allegedly. the UN ambassador
is setting up a multinational

1406
01:17:45.822 --> 01:17:48.825
Godzilla strike force
with the Security Council.

1407
01:17:48.908 --> 01:17:51.911
Will the U.S. go through with it?

1408
01:17:51.995 --> 01:17:54.247
Looks like it.

1409
01:17:55.123 --> 01:17:57.292
Yokota and the U.S. team have concluded

1410
01:17:57.375 --> 01:18:00.670
that the only option is a nuclear attack
using ballistic missiles.

1411
01:18:00.753 --> 01:18:02.297
Apparently. it's started.

1412
01:18:02.380 --> 01:18:04.674
The Pentagon's already working
on setting the explosive yield

1413
01:18:04.757 --> 01:18:07.302
for a B83 nuclear warhead.

1414
01:18:10.054 --> 01:18:12.223
They're planning on using it on Tokyo?

1415
01:18:12.307 --> 01:18:15.226
I was ordered to evacuate right away.

1416
01:18:16.978 --> 01:18:19.022
Hold on.

1417
01:18:19.105 --> 01:18:23.151
So you're saying it's decided?

1418
01:18:28.281 --> 01:18:30.742
But I'm not gonna do that.

1419
01:18:33.244 --> 01:18:36.122
My grandmother lived through
two atomic bombs.

1420
01:18:36.873 --> 01:18:40.126
I refuse to witness a third bomb dropped
on her country.

1421
01:18:40.209 --> 01:18:42.003
I won't let it happen.

1422
01:18:45.673 --> 01:18:47.342
Certainly. yes.

1423
01:18:47.425 --> 01:18:51.179
Then we'll go ahead and act accordingly.
President Ross.

1424
01:19:04.525 --> 01:19:06.569
Well. you heard it.

1425
01:19:07.570 --> 01:19:11.574
That country really does force
some unreasonable demands on us.

1426
01:19:11.658 --> 01:19:14.160
This is too much.

1427
01:19:16.329 --> 01:19:18.998
How can we stand for this?!

1428
01:19:19.082 --> 01:19:20.583
I agree.

1429
01:19:21.668 --> 01:19:23.127
Call the Chief Cabinet Secretary.

1430
01:19:23.211 --> 01:19:24.462
Right.

1431
01:19:27.048 --> 01:19:31.010
The UN Security Council passed
a resolution to form a multinational force

1432
01:19:31.094 --> 01:19:34.347
centered on the U.S. military...

1433
01:19:34.430 --> 01:19:37.600
to exterminate Gojira once and for all.

1434
01:19:39.018 --> 01:19:43.523
As party to the resolution
and participant.

1435
01:19:43.606 --> 01:19:47.860
the Japanese nation will be under
their command.

1436
01:19:47.944 --> 01:19:50.279
In other words...

1437
01:19:51.614 --> 01:19:55.660
...I am going to need special legislation
delegating full authority

1438
01:19:55.743 --> 01:19:57.453
to the Prime Minister.

1439
01:20:05.628 --> 01:20:08.423
This legislation...

1440
01:20:08.506 --> 01:20:12.010
it'll also authorize the use
of a nuclear weapon?

1441
01:20:29.444 --> 01:20:31.279
I didn't want this.

1442
01:20:31.362 --> 01:20:34.323
This'll be how I go down in history.

1443
01:20:40.997 --> 01:20:44.459
From here on. the U.S. will be
in charge of exterminating Gojira.

1444
01:20:44.542 --> 01:20:46.335
under UN jurisdiction.

1445
01:20:49.964 --> 01:20:54.177
After the war.
Japan became a tributary state.

1446
01:20:54.260 --> 01:20:57.138
The postwar period will continue forever.

1447
01:20:57.221 --> 01:20:59.599
You're just giving up then?

1448
01:21:03.936 --> 01:21:06.147
A direct hit from a thermonuclear weapon.

1449
01:21:06.230 --> 01:21:10.151
No living creature could possibly
withstand that million-degree heat.

1450
01:21:10.234 --> 01:21:15.823
If we want to completely eradicate it
then a nuclear attack is the right choice.

1451
01:21:15.907 --> 01:21:18.951
But we're on the verge of a breakthrough
with our freezing method.

1452
01:21:19.035 --> 01:21:21.204
Please reconsider.

1453
01:21:21.287 --> 01:21:24.248
But your plan has too many unknowns
at the end of the day.

1454
01:21:24.332 --> 01:21:27.168
Besides. if we move forward
with the nuclear attack.

1455
01:21:27.251 --> 01:21:29.504
the countries from around the world have
already pledged their support

1456
01:21:29.587 --> 01:21:31.881
to assist us
in the nation's reconstruction.

1457
01:21:31.964 --> 01:21:35.718
If we can't completely dispose of Gojira
while the world is looking to us.

1458
01:21:35.802 --> 01:21:39.055
then we risk our nation losing
their trust for good.

1459
01:21:39.138 --> 01:21:42.308
We have no choice
but to rely on this nuclear attack.

1460
01:21:43.309 --> 01:21:45.686
You know what my job is?

1461
01:21:45.770 --> 01:21:47.605
To look to the future.

1462
01:21:47.688 --> 01:21:50.608
To consider what will happen
to our country after Gojira is eradicated.

1463
01:21:50.691 --> 01:21:53.319
The damage has only affected
three wards so far.

1464
01:21:53.402 --> 01:21:54.737
meaning Tokyo can still be rebuilt.

1465
01:21:54.821 --> 01:21:56.989
Using nuclear weapons
will make that difficult.

1466
01:21:57.073 --> 01:21:59.325
The city's economy is already
virtually nonexistent.

1467
01:21:59.408 --> 01:22:01.369
With bond and stock prices
continuing to plummet.

1468
01:22:01.452 --> 01:22:03.037
and the yen weakening as we speak.

1469
01:22:03.121 --> 01:22:06.249
rebuilding will be impossible
if the nation defaults.

1470
01:22:06.332 --> 01:22:08.251
You don't realize. that what we need

1471
01:22:08.334 --> 01:22:10.670
is international funding and sympathy
to survive.

1472
01:22:12.505 --> 01:22:14.674
So your first priority is reconstruction?

1473
01:22:14.757 --> 01:22:17.718
To save the country.

1474
01:22:19.387 --> 01:22:21.556
We have to do whatever it takes.

1475
01:22:23.683 --> 01:22:25.268
Yaguchi...

1476
01:22:25.351 --> 01:22:26.978
wake up.

1477
01:22:27.061 --> 01:22:29.564
This is our reality.

1478
01:22:31.190 --> 01:22:33.609
Did you say a nuclear attack on Gojira?

1479
01:22:33.693 --> 01:22:35.194
Their bombing our country?!

1480
01:22:35.278 --> 01:22:38.197
The government just approved it
and they already notified the UN.

1481
01:22:38.281 --> 01:22:39.949
But that's insane.

1482
01:22:40.032 --> 01:22:42.034
Gojira has transcended evolution.

1483
01:22:42.118 --> 01:22:44.495
How do we know it hasn't
conquered death itself?

1484
01:22:44.579 --> 01:22:47.999
So the only two ways to end this
is Yaguchi Plan's coagulation

1485
01:22:48.082 --> 01:22:49.500
or incinerate it with a nuke.

1486
01:22:49.584 --> 01:22:52.628
While it's true that we could choose
to use the nuke...

1487
01:22:52.712 --> 01:22:54.547
that doesn't mean we should.

1488
01:22:54.630 --> 01:22:57.758
Who's the real threat to us.
man or Gojira?

1489
01:22:57.842 --> 01:22:59.844
The UN will want to begin
the nuclear attack right away.

1490
01:22:59.927 --> 01:23:02.555
However. they'll likely evacuate
all the Tokyo residents first.

1491
01:23:02.638 --> 01:23:05.057
That gives us our window
for finishing our work here.

1492
01:23:05.141 --> 01:23:07.143
That's right.
Through the sample experiments.

1493
01:23:07.226 --> 01:23:09.562
we were able to determine
the most effective substance.

1494
01:23:09.645 --> 01:23:11.022
Now comes production.

1495
01:23:11.105 --> 01:23:13.274
Based on the estimated
blood volume of Gojira.

1496
01:23:13.357 --> 01:23:16.360
we'll need at least 672 kiloliters
of coagulant.

1497
01:23:16.444 --> 01:23:18.696
We're securing plants nationwide
for production.

1498
01:23:18.779 --> 01:23:19.780
Will we make it?

1499
01:23:19.864 --> 01:23:21.949
Of course we'll make it! We have to!

1500
01:23:22.033 --> 01:23:23.910
Don't give up now!

1501
01:23:23.993 --> 01:23:26.162
Don't abandon our country
when we still have time!

1502
01:23:26.245 --> 01:23:27.914
As many production lines as we can get.

1503
01:23:27.997 --> 01:23:30.041
We need every private chemical company
across the country on this.

1504
01:23:30.124 --> 01:23:32.043
If anyone can get it done. you can.

1505
01:23:32.126 --> 01:23:34.378
I'll send over all the pertinent data
to your researcher.

1506
01:23:34.462 --> 01:23:37.215
so ask the director to send a
simplified draft of the production process

1507
01:23:37.298 --> 01:23:38.633
as soon as they can.

1508
01:23:38.716 --> 01:23:40.218
Thanks to the samples
being scattered around.

1509
01:23:40.301 --> 01:23:41.469
we're getting broad cross-checking.

1510
01:23:41.552 --> 01:23:43.554
Interesting. sharing our data worked.

1511
01:23:56.734 --> 01:23:59.028
Please have the police and MLIT
work out the logistics

1512
01:23:59.111 --> 01:24:00.780
for the local transport of coagulants.

1513
01:24:00.863 --> 01:24:02.031
Okay. I'll get on that.

1514
01:24:02.114 --> 01:24:04.784
And in return. I need the METI
to coordinate pump makers.

1515
01:24:05.993 --> 01:24:08.579
A company in Shanghai's willing
to give us three tankers.

1516
01:24:08.663 --> 01:24:11.165
Just as long as we agree
to give them back when we're finished.

1517
01:24:11.249 --> 01:24:14.543
That's not a concern. We just need five
wheel loaders. it doesn't matter the size.

1518
01:24:19.131 --> 01:24:22.260
Ambassador Lansing has informed us
of the multinational forces estimate

1519
01:24:22.343 --> 01:24:25.763
on the amount of energy Gojira released
during the last battle.

1520
01:24:25.846 --> 01:24:27.723
They project the creature's energy beam

1521
01:24:27.807 --> 01:24:30.643
will be back to full power
within 360 hours.

1522
01:24:32.520 --> 01:24:37.191
In other words. it's likely Gojira's
activity will resume in 15 days.

1523
01:24:38.276 --> 01:24:39.360
I see.

1524
01:25:05.636 --> 01:25:07.221
Evacuation.

1525
01:25:07.305 --> 01:25:11.267
That means forcing residents to abandon
everything they've ever known.

1526
01:25:12.852 --> 01:25:15.396
This isn't an easy decision.

1527
01:25:15.479 --> 01:25:16.897
I agree. sir.

1528
01:25:16.981 --> 01:25:19.775
Evacuate 3.6 million citizens.
It's impossible.

1529
01:25:19.859 --> 01:25:21.944
Even the police can't carry out
an operation on that scale.

1530
01:25:22.028 --> 01:25:24.155
Not only Tokyo. but Chiba and Kanagawa
are also affected.

1531
01:25:24.238 --> 01:25:25.489
Too many residents are involved here.

1532
01:25:25.614 --> 01:25:28.159
Governor Kozuka strongly protests
the sacrifice of Tokyo.

1533
01:25:28.242 --> 01:25:30.328
This is an important national decision.

1534
01:25:30.411 --> 01:25:31.787
It isn't a municipal one.

1535
01:25:31.871 --> 01:25:34.707
Relocation selection and approvals
won't be completed in time.

1536
01:25:34.790 --> 01:25:36.208
Two weeks isn't enough.

1537
01:25:36.292 --> 01:25:38.669
The moment that Gojira resumes
activity again

1538
01:25:38.753 --> 01:25:42.173
is the moment that the thermonuclear
attack will be moved up unconditionally.

1539
01:25:42.256 --> 01:25:44.216
Casualties will be unavoidable.
I'm afraid.

1540
01:25:44.300 --> 01:25:46.969
because. at that time.
ballistic missiles will be launched

1541
01:25:47.053 --> 01:25:49.555
from a strategic nuclear submarine at us.

1542
01:25:49.638 --> 01:25:52.058
as per the decision
of the international coalition.

1543
01:25:52.141 --> 01:25:53.642
Damn it!

1544
01:25:53.726 --> 01:25:56.479
Yeah. easy for them to say
since we're all the way over in Asia!

1545
01:25:56.562 --> 01:25:58.981
If it were in New York.
they'd do the same thing.

1546
01:25:59.065 --> 01:26:01.734
Their decision was made
regardless of where we are.

1547
01:26:06.238 --> 01:26:07.656
Children come first!

1548
01:26:07.740 --> 01:26:09.283
Parents. please don't let go
of your children's hands at any time!

1549
01:26:09.367 --> 01:26:11.660
Hey. where are we going?

1550
01:26:38.187 --> 01:26:40.689
Land prices in western Japan are soaring.

1551
01:26:40.773 --> 01:26:42.733
And food's in short supply.

1552
01:26:42.817 --> 01:26:45.861
Companies and shops
in the Kanto area are shuttered.

1553
01:26:45.945 --> 01:26:48.155
City's full of unemployed citizens.

1554
01:26:49.281 --> 01:26:52.910
The yen's also continuing to weaken.
reflecting investors' fears.

1555
01:26:52.993 --> 01:26:55.538
Well. some people are profiting from it.

1556
01:26:55.579 --> 01:26:59.125
There are all kinds of individuals.
in this world.

1557
01:27:00.584 --> 01:27:02.503
You got any information that's not online?

1558
01:27:02.586 --> 01:27:05.798
Of course. It's what I do. after all.

1559
01:27:05.881 --> 01:27:09.051
In exchange for this.
I need you to promise one thing.

1560
01:27:09.135 --> 01:27:12.513
Print my article one day before
the nuclear attack.

1561
01:27:14.098 --> 01:27:16.976
I have new info on Gojira.

1562
01:27:17.059 --> 01:27:20.980
In exchange. the announcement timing
is for us to decide.

1563
01:27:21.063 --> 01:27:22.940
How's that sound?

1564
01:27:23.023 --> 01:27:25.818
Yeah. yeah. I get it.

1565
01:27:30.322 --> 01:27:32.992
It seems the professor resented
the radiation sickness

1566
01:27:33.075 --> 01:27:35.911
that ultimately took his wife's life.

1567
01:27:36.537 --> 01:27:42.251
So that's why he continued his research
into neutralizing radioactive material.

1568
01:27:42.334 --> 01:27:44.378
If it's possible to neutralize
radioactive material.

1569
01:27:44.462 --> 01:27:47.423
it's also possible to create
new radioactive material.

1570
01:27:47.506 --> 01:27:49.925
He must have feared
that it would be used by the military.

1571
01:27:50.009 --> 01:27:53.304
That would explain why he chose to redact
so much of the DOE data.

1572
01:27:53.387 --> 01:27:56.849
He hated radioactive material.

1573
01:27:56.932 --> 01:28:01.520
And he probably hated anyone
who was involved in its creation.

1574
01:28:02.438 --> 01:28:07.193
Japan left his wife to die.
so it was no exception.

1575
01:28:07.276 --> 01:28:11.447
And yet. he purposefully left behind
his data and wrote. "Do as you like."

1576
01:28:11.530 --> 01:28:13.073
What a strange person.

1577
01:28:15.451 --> 01:28:18.037
So what did he end up choosing to do?

1578
01:28:27.630 --> 01:28:29.089
Thank you for the meal.

1579
01:28:31.926 --> 01:28:34.178
Any luck on solving the chart?

1580
01:28:34.261 --> 01:28:36.555
Not even with help from
the encryption specialist department

1581
01:28:36.639 --> 01:28:38.307
over at Intelligence and Research.

1582
01:28:38.390 --> 01:28:39.767
Are there any updates from the U.S.?

1583
01:28:39.850 --> 01:28:41.852
Haven't heard anything concrete so far.

1584
01:28:41.936 --> 01:28:43.229
It's best not to rely on them.

1585
01:28:43.312 --> 01:28:45.981
We regard it as significant data
for some kind of multitiered approach

1586
01:28:46.065 --> 01:28:48.108
related to Gojira.
yet there's still more to it.

1587
01:28:48.192 --> 01:28:49.652
Rather than a chemical schematic.

1588
01:28:49.735 --> 01:28:51.820
it looks more like a conceptual pattern.
or mandala.

1589
01:28:51.904 --> 01:28:53.906
It's a paradoxical question
that can't be solved

1590
01:28:53.948 --> 01:28:55.658
unless you can imagine the answer first.

1591
01:28:55.741 --> 01:28:57.993
Professor Maki was a little twisted.

1592
01:28:59.578 --> 01:29:01.664
Even I don't get the meaning
of these lines.

1593
01:29:01.747 --> 01:29:05.167
Why'd he put it on paper and not data.
is my question.

1594
01:29:05.251 --> 01:29:08.963
Well. perhaps it should be folded.

1595
01:29:11.882 --> 01:29:14.802
You know. Gojira's so huge.

1596
01:29:14.885 --> 01:29:17.137
it doesn't look like it could fill up
on radioactive waste.

1597
01:29:17.221 --> 01:29:18.847
I bet it's always hungry.

1598
01:29:18.931 --> 01:29:20.015
No doubt.

1599
01:29:20.099 --> 01:29:23.143
And what's funny
is that its teeth are all misaligned.

1600
01:29:23.227 --> 01:29:25.854
You wouldn't think it could eat
nuclear waste like this.

1601
01:29:31.610 --> 01:29:33.529
Origami.

1602
01:29:37.408 --> 01:29:38.993
The waste isn't eaten.

1603
01:29:39.076 --> 01:29:40.911
<i>By folding the paper
into two origami shapes.</i>

1604
01:29:40.995 --> 01:29:42.371
<i>new information is revealed to us</i>

1605
01:29:42.454 --> 01:29:43.914
<i>and we're able to grasp
the entire pattern.</i>

1606
01:29:43.998 --> 01:29:45.124
<i>As a result...</i>

1607
01:29:45.207 --> 01:29:47.751
<i>We were too fixated on radioactive
material being the energy source.</i>

1608
01:29:47.876 --> 01:29:49.920
What Professor Maki left behind.

1609
01:29:50.004 --> 01:29:52.298
is a molecular chart
for converting elements in the body.

1610
01:29:52.381 --> 01:29:54.842
Element conversion molecules.

1611
01:29:54.925 --> 01:29:56.760
The unknown radioactive isotope
detected earlier.

1612
01:29:56.844 --> 01:29:59.013
its very existence. that's the proof.

1613
01:29:59.096 --> 01:30:01.724
Substances with few protons.
such as hydrogen or nitrogen.

1614
01:30:01.807 --> 01:30:04.685
are passed through the cell membrane
to convert the elements inside the cell

1615
01:30:04.768 --> 01:30:06.186
into the necessary molecules.

1616
01:30:06.270 --> 01:30:07.938
We can assume that Gojira is a mixotroph

1617
01:30:08.022 --> 01:30:11.525
with a thermonuclear energy conversion
organ that uses the heat from the decay.

1618
01:30:11.609 --> 01:30:13.819
It's a bold theory but within reason.

1619
01:30:13.902 --> 01:30:16.739
It can live anywhere as long
as there's water and oxygen.

1620
01:30:16.822 --> 01:30:19.283
Like an ascetic surviving on mist.

1621
01:30:19.366 --> 01:30:22.453
To sum it all up. Gojira's a threat
to humanity's existence

1622
01:30:22.536 --> 01:30:25.831
yet also poses a revelation of infinite
physical possibilities all at once.

1623
01:30:25.914 --> 01:30:27.041
Did I get that right?

1624
01:30:27.124 --> 01:30:29.043
But then we're facing the possibility
that the blood coagulant

1625
01:30:29.126 --> 01:30:31.920
will be neutralized in its body
and therefore prove to be ineffective.

1626
01:30:32.004 --> 01:30:33.547
The Yaguchi Plan could fall through.

1627
01:30:33.631 --> 01:30:35.424
If that's the case. what should we do?

1628
01:30:35.507 --> 01:30:36.634
We raise its certainty of working.

1629
01:30:36.717 --> 01:30:38.135
The Yaguchi Plan is all we have.
after all.

1630
01:30:38.218 --> 01:30:40.220
First of all. we have to analyze
this molecular structure

1631
01:30:40.304 --> 01:30:42.139
and find a way around it.
Ready for the analysis?

1632
01:30:42.222 --> 01:30:44.808
Supercomputers all over Japan have already
started running parallel analysis

1633
01:30:44.892 --> 01:30:47.978
under our initiative. however. how many
days will it take to get the results?

1634
01:30:48.062 --> 01:30:50.481
We only have ten days left
before the nuclear attack.

1635
01:30:50.564 --> 01:30:54.068
That's why I asked the MEXT to use
their global connections on our behalf.

1636
01:30:54.151 --> 01:30:56.570
We've received a call from Japan.

1637
01:30:56.654 --> 01:30:58.280
They're asking to connect
our supercomputers

1638
01:30:58.364 --> 01:31:00.074
in parallel to help analyze Godzilla.

1639
01:31:00.157 --> 01:31:01.575
Under no circumstances can we do that.

1640
01:31:01.659 --> 01:31:04.119
If we open up our closed system
to foreign countries.

1641
01:31:04.203 --> 01:31:05.746
we might as well publish
our research data online.

1642
01:31:05.829 --> 01:31:08.874
We should tell them that we're
very sorry. but our hands are tied here.

1643
01:31:08.957 --> 01:31:10.876
Oh. just take a deep breath and calm down.

1644
01:31:10.959 --> 01:31:14.380
I think we can have faith in the Japanese.
don't you? Hmm?

1645
01:31:14.463 --> 01:31:19.218
Go ahead and tell them we'd be happy
to support them at this time.

1646
01:31:30.646 --> 01:31:33.107
- We've solved Professor Maki's riddle!
- Huh?

1647
01:31:33.190 --> 01:31:35.150
Oh. Let me see.

1648
01:31:35.234 --> 01:31:37.569
- What?
- Let me see. let me see. let me see.

1649
01:31:38.237 --> 01:31:39.363
Here.

1650
01:31:39.446 --> 01:31:41.657
Hey. wait. wait.

1651
01:31:41.740 --> 01:31:43.242
Extraordinary.

1652
01:31:43.325 --> 01:31:45.869
As you can see.
It's not the cell membrane itself.

1653
01:31:45.953 --> 01:31:48.288
It's actually the molecular structure
of an extremophile

1654
01:31:48.372 --> 01:31:51.542
that inhibits the activity
of the cell membrane.

1655
01:31:53.711 --> 01:31:57.339
If we also administer this inhibitor. it
could ensure the success of the coagulant.

1656
01:31:57.423 --> 01:31:59.258
Freezing Gojira's possible. after all.

1657
01:32:01.385 --> 01:32:03.137
Looks promising.

1658
01:32:05.139 --> 01:32:06.932
Okay.

1659
01:32:10.060 --> 01:32:12.896
Professor Maki likely anticipated
all of this.

1660
01:32:13.939 --> 01:32:19.027
He may have wanted to unleash the power
of a raging god as some kind of test.

1661
01:32:19.111 --> 01:32:23.490
To test humanity. this country
and the Japanese people.

1662
01:32:23.532 --> 01:32:28.454
His note said to do whatever we want. and
that includes the use of nuclear weapons.

1663
01:32:29.496 --> 01:32:31.123
That's right.

1664
01:32:32.166 --> 01:32:34.460
He did say to do what we want.

1665
01:32:37.212 --> 01:32:39.006
But still...

1666
01:32:39.089 --> 01:32:42.801
getting your way in this country
is difficult.

1667
01:32:44.511 --> 01:32:45.846
You're right.

1668
01:32:47.055 --> 01:32:48.390
Especially alone.

1669
01:32:48.474 --> 01:32:49.850
Here's the latest.

1670
01:32:49.933 --> 01:32:52.227
It sounds like the last kinks
in the Yaguchi Plan are being ironed out

1671
01:32:52.311 --> 01:32:53.645
even as we speak.

1672
01:32:53.729 --> 01:32:56.690
I'd like to once again
ask for your approval to deploy it.

1673
01:32:56.774 --> 01:32:59.359
I understand. Izumi.

1674
01:32:59.443 --> 01:33:02.529
but a UN resolution
has already been passed.

1675
01:33:02.613 --> 01:33:05.532
Some say that the U.S. is trying
to bring this to an early close

1676
01:33:05.657 --> 01:33:09.119
in order to obscure the fact that they've
been concealing Gojira's existence.

1677
01:33:09.203 --> 01:33:11.955
We're already well aware of all of that.

1678
01:33:12.039 --> 01:33:15.083
You understand our country's
current position. don't you?

1679
01:33:15.167 --> 01:33:16.502
Of course I do.

1680
01:33:16.585 --> 01:33:20.881
Saving another country from embarrassment
shouldn't come at the cost of our country.

1681
01:33:23.091 --> 01:33:28.931
So what you're saying is we should honor
the principle of human rights.

1682
01:33:29.014 --> 01:33:31.058
Prime Minister.

1683
01:33:31.141 --> 01:33:33.519
perhaps we should start doing
what we want to do.

1684
01:33:34.603 --> 01:33:36.522
You're right.

1685
01:33:37.523 --> 01:33:40.692
So. where do I. uh. put my stamp?

1686
01:33:43.487 --> 01:33:46.949
The purpose is to freeze the activity
of the Giant Unidentified Life-Form.

1687
01:33:47.032 --> 01:33:50.911
Operational guidelines centered on the
oral administration of a blood coagulant.

1688
01:33:50.994 --> 01:33:52.788
It's long-winded

1689
01:33:54.414 --> 01:33:55.999
This is the government. after all.

1690
01:33:56.083 --> 01:33:59.002
It's childish to call it
the Gojira Freezing Operation.

1691
01:33:59.086 --> 01:34:00.921
Why not Operation Yashiori?

1692
01:34:01.004 --> 01:34:03.090
Make it so.

1693
01:34:03.173 --> 01:34:04.967
This will be carried out in five stages.

1694
01:34:05.050 --> 01:34:07.219
Asaka has worked out the details already.

1695
01:34:07.302 --> 01:34:09.137
Remote vehicle operation training.

1696
01:34:09.221 --> 01:34:11.056
restoration of
the overhead infrastructure.

1697
01:34:11.139 --> 01:34:13.475
and explosive drills
have all been completed.

1698
01:34:13.559 --> 01:34:15.477
All that's left is execution.

1699
01:34:16.562 --> 01:34:18.188
Thank you all very much.

1700
01:34:18.272 --> 01:34:19.773
No need to thank us.

1701
01:34:19.857 --> 01:34:21.400
This is our work.

1702
01:34:31.118 --> 01:34:33.787
Only two days left on the countdown.

1703
01:34:35.497 --> 01:34:37.374
Ah. damn it.

1704
01:34:37.457 --> 01:34:38.834
It'll take another three days
to secure the production

1705
01:34:38.917 --> 01:34:40.919
of the minimum amount of inhibitor.

1706
01:34:41.003 --> 01:34:43.255
Is there any way we can suspend
the 24-hour countdown?

1707
01:34:43.338 --> 01:34:45.799
Then we have to think of how
we can delay the Security Council.

1708
01:34:45.883 --> 01:34:47.175
Who can help us stall?

1709
01:34:47.259 --> 01:34:49.219
China and Russia are out...
they're pushing for the attack.

1710
01:34:49.303 --> 01:34:50.554
They're too close geopolitically.

1711
01:34:50.637 --> 01:34:51.638
What about France?

1712
01:34:51.722 --> 01:34:53.181
They're a nuclear power.

1713
01:34:53.265 --> 01:34:55.142
I think they'd be interested
in Gojira's biology.

1714
01:34:55.225 --> 01:34:56.351
Hmm. right.

1715
01:34:56.435 --> 01:34:58.395
I have connections over there.
Let me reach out to them.

1716
01:34:58.478 --> 01:34:59.688
Yes. please.

1717
01:34:59.771 --> 01:35:01.773
I'll also contact
the European Bureau Chief.

1718
01:35:01.857 --> 01:35:04.234
That'd be great.
I'll talk to Foreign Minister Katayama.

1719
01:35:04.318 --> 01:35:05.903
Secure 24 more hours at all costs.

1720
01:35:05.986 --> 01:35:07.321
Understood.

1721
01:36:45.002 --> 01:36:47.170
<i>A joint operation with the U.S. military?</i>

1722
01:36:47.254 --> 01:36:49.715
The success rate will be higher
than if the SDF acted alone.

1723
01:36:49.798 --> 01:36:53.093
What about each side's command units.
will they be able to coordinate that?

1724
01:36:53.176 --> 01:36:55.053
This country's well-liked. you know.

1725
01:36:55.137 --> 01:36:58.140
It already looks like you'll get support
from the Marines and the Air Force.

1726
01:36:58.223 --> 01:37:00.308
We've even secured extra drones.
if you need 'em.

1727
01:37:00.392 --> 01:37:02.394
So. what do you say?

1728
01:37:02.477 --> 01:37:03.812
I'm in.

1729
01:37:18.493 --> 01:37:20.620
We've scraped together the minimum amount
of inhibitor somehow.

1730
01:37:20.704 --> 01:37:21.705
That's right.

1731
01:37:21.788 --> 01:37:24.916
Please send some tankers to SB in Tsukuba
as soon as possible.

1732
01:37:27.794 --> 01:37:30.088
All of the necessary materials and
coagulant are ready to be transported

1733
01:37:30.172 --> 01:37:31.590
for the start of the operation.

1734
01:37:31.673 --> 01:37:33.633
Go ahead and give the green light to HQ.

1735
01:37:34.760 --> 01:37:36.344
Deputy Chief
I urge you to please reconsider

1736
01:37:36.428 --> 01:37:38.847
accompanying the troops
on the front line.

1737
01:37:38.930 --> 01:37:42.184
I have a feeling the situation will likely
call for a political decision to be made.

1738
01:37:42.267 --> 01:37:44.436
They'll need someone
who can do that instantly.

1739
01:37:44.519 --> 01:37:46.021
It's still too dangerous.

1740
01:37:46.104 --> 01:37:48.106
Policymakers don't have
to lead the charge.

1741
01:37:48.190 --> 01:37:50.067
Didn't you want to be PM in ten years?

1742
01:37:50.150 --> 01:37:52.360
But we have to ensure
Japan's still around in ten years.

1743
01:37:52.444 --> 01:37:54.362
That's more important
than being its leader.

1744
01:37:54.446 --> 01:37:56.031
We've got young talent.

1745
01:37:56.114 --> 01:37:58.200
They're in various sectors.
public and private.

1746
01:37:58.283 --> 01:38:01.620
And with you here. finding the next leader
won't be a problem.

1747
01:38:06.875 --> 01:38:09.377
You've helped me stay the course.
Thank you.

1748
01:38:09.461 --> 01:38:11.963
That's absurd.
You should be thanking Akasaka.

1749
01:38:12.047 --> 01:38:13.548
I'll leave the rest to you.

1750
01:38:13.632 --> 01:38:14.883
Yeah.

1751
01:38:14.966 --> 01:38:17.177
Save me Party Secretary.

1752
01:38:34.611 --> 01:38:37.739
When carrying out
this Yashiori Operation...

1753
01:38:40.575 --> 01:38:46.164
...there's a very real possibility that
you will risk acute radiation exposure!

1754
01:38:50.127 --> 01:38:52.921
Those who are here.
aren't guaranteed to leave here alive!

1755
01:38:54.756 --> 01:38:58.051
Yet we must see this to the end!

1756
01:39:02.097 --> 01:39:06.351
We are here to show the whole world
this country's greatest strength!

1757
01:39:08.353 --> 01:39:10.772
The SDF now has the opportunity

1758
01:39:10.856 --> 01:39:14.192
to be the last line of the defense
against this great threat!

1759
01:39:20.740 --> 01:39:22.826
The world's relying on you...

1760
01:39:22.909 --> 01:39:25.453
and so is the future of Japan!

1761
01:39:27.372 --> 01:39:28.874
Do your best!

1762
01:39:29.958 --> 01:39:31.668
Right! Roll out!

1763
01:39:31.751 --> 01:39:33.420
Yes. sir!

1764
01:39:37.757 --> 01:39:40.010
Northwest wind. two meters.

1765
01:39:40.093 --> 01:39:42.596
The creature's plume
is heading toward Tokyo Bay.

1766
01:39:42.679 --> 01:39:45.056
Damage is estimated to be minimal.

1767
01:39:45.140 --> 01:39:47.309
All units. In position. Standing by.

1768
01:39:47.392 --> 01:39:49.311
Contact from U.S. military headquarters.

1769
01:39:49.394 --> 01:39:51.897
U.S. attack drone squadron airborne
in designated holding patterns.

1770
01:39:51.980 --> 01:39:53.315
No problems.

1771
01:39:53.398 --> 01:39:55.567
All systems are go.
Awaiting your orders. sir.

1772
01:39:55.650 --> 01:39:58.987
But we still haven't received word
from Tokyo of the evacuation.

1773
01:39:59.070 --> 01:40:00.363
We've got one shot.

1774
01:40:00.447 --> 01:40:02.657
We can't miss this opportunity.
Let's continue.

1775
01:40:02.741 --> 01:40:06.036
Tell the local governments to enforce
curfew order. Commander Tanba.

1776
01:40:06.119 --> 01:40:07.204
Roger that.

1777
01:40:07.287 --> 01:40:09.414
Alert each local government
in the Kanto region.

1778
01:40:09.497 --> 01:40:12.042
Have them issue a 50-hour indoor
confinement curfew for all citizens.

1779
01:40:12.125 --> 01:40:14.211
Everyone is to refrain from going out.

1780
01:40:14.294 --> 01:40:15.337
Roger that!

1781
01:40:15.420 --> 01:40:16.504
Contact from Shimbashi.

1782
01:40:16.588 --> 01:40:20.008
All unmanned vehicles have been detached.
Passing zero point.

1783
01:40:20.091 --> 01:40:22.093
Now. commence Operation Yashiori.

1784
01:40:22.219 --> 01:40:24.596
Phase One. Diversion. begin!

1785
01:40:42.739 --> 01:40:45.617
Diversion success! Train blasts effective!

1786
01:40:45.700 --> 01:40:47.202
Operation. Phase Two.

1787
01:40:47.285 --> 01:40:48.787
Commence air force attack.

1788
01:40:48.870 --> 01:40:50.580
Roger that. Contact U.S. forces.

1789
01:41:05.595 --> 01:41:09.266
The target is discharging photons
from its dorsal fins!

1790
01:41:09.349 --> 01:41:10.725
It's taking down the drones.

1791
01:41:10.809 --> 01:41:12.269
Everything's going according to plan.

1792
01:41:13.895 --> 01:41:15.647
First drone sortie destroyed.

1793
01:41:15.730 --> 01:41:17.565
No matter. We'll wear it down.

1794
01:41:17.649 --> 01:41:20.485
We have to keep Gojira emitting radiation
until it's spent.

1795
01:41:24.906 --> 01:41:27.117
<i>Second drone sortie. all destroyed.</i>

1796
01:41:27.200 --> 01:41:29.160
<i>Third drone sortie. commencing attack!</i>

1797
01:41:29.244 --> 01:41:31.329
<i>Target. moving to kill point one.</i>

1798
01:41:37.836 --> 01:41:39.462
Third sortie. destroyed!

1799
01:41:41.631 --> 01:41:43.425
The contamination zone is growing.

1800
01:41:43.508 --> 01:41:46.052
Deputy Chief. the radiation dose
will exceed the planned area.

1801
01:41:46.136 --> 01:41:48.555
If we stop now.
all of this will have been for nothing.

1802
01:41:48.638 --> 01:41:50.515
Please continue the attack.

1803
01:42:00.567 --> 01:42:02.360
Fourth sortie. destroyed!

1804
01:42:02.444 --> 01:42:04.112
We can't let up. Launch the fifth sortie.

1805
01:42:10.577 --> 01:42:13.079
Target has stopped discharging its beam
from its dorsal fins.

1806
01:42:13.163 --> 01:42:15.123
Fifth sortie. still engaging the target.

1807
01:42:22.005 --> 01:42:23.757
How can it do that?

1808
01:42:30.096 --> 01:42:31.681
Fifth sortie. destroyed.

1809
01:42:33.600 --> 01:42:36.436
Gojira's plume.
it exceeds twice the expected size.

1810
01:42:36.519 --> 01:42:38.146
Stay strong. We have to endure.

1811
01:42:38.229 --> 01:42:40.023
Sixth sortie. commence attack!

1812
01:42:48.782 --> 01:42:50.450
The volume of radiation is decreasing.

1813
01:42:56.456 --> 01:42:58.416
Confirming that the target's flame
has ceased.

1814
01:42:58.500 --> 01:43:00.627
Target luring to kill point one complete.

1815
01:43:00.710 --> 01:43:02.295
Okay. onto Phase Three.

1816
01:43:02.379 --> 01:43:04.005
Commence stationary blasting.

1817
01:43:04.089 --> 01:43:05.215
Ignite!

1818
01:43:31.658 --> 01:43:33.827
Volume of radiation has fallen
to expected value.

1819
01:43:33.910 --> 01:43:35.787
Fixing target at kill point one.

1820
01:43:35.870 --> 01:43:37.247
Roger that. Phase Four.

1821
01:43:37.330 --> 01:43:39.040
Guided blast. commence!

1822
01:44:12.323 --> 01:44:13.533
The target has fallen!

1823
01:44:13.616 --> 01:44:15.201
Kill point one. fixing complete.

1824
01:44:15.285 --> 01:44:16.828
Operation in the final phase.

1825
01:44:16.911 --> 01:44:18.872
Special crane platoon. Commence!

1826
01:44:18.955 --> 01:44:21.499
Roger that! 1st platoon. forward!

1827
01:44:25.086 --> 01:44:28.923
<i>Crane Platoon 01.
Hydra-slayer 01. move out!</i>

1828
01:44:29.007 --> 01:44:32.343
<i>Cranes 12 to 14.
move to combat formation behind BP2.</i>

1829
01:44:33.011 --> 01:44:37.056
<i>Hydra-slayer 01. Crane 11.
and BP1 in the deployment zone.</i>

1830
01:44:37.140 --> 01:44:39.601
<i>Crane 11. Hydra-slayer 01. Roger that!</i>

1831
01:44:39.684 --> 01:44:41.811
<i>Standby in defensive circle
with engines ready.</i>

1832
01:44:41.895 --> 01:44:44.063
<i>All special vehicles.
deploy outriggers and approach BP1.</i>

1833
01:44:44.147 --> 01:44:46.316
<i>After that. commence injection.</i>

1834
01:44:46.399 --> 01:44:48.193
<i>Crane 12 and BP2. deployment complete.</i>

1835
01:44:48.276 --> 01:44:50.653
<i>Hydra-slayer 01. Crane 15.</i>

1836
01:44:50.737 --> 01:44:52.614
<i>All 15 vehicles. deployed.</i>

1837
01:44:52.697 --> 01:44:53.990
<i>Starting connection. Over.</i>

1838
01:44:54.073 --> 01:44:57.452
<i>Crane 15. Hydra-slayer 01. Roger that.</i>

1839
01:44:57.535 --> 01:44:58.870
<i>Stay at outer operation range.</i>

1840
01:45:02.415 --> 01:45:03.791
All units. commence injection!

1841
01:45:03.875 --> 01:45:05.710
Inject the coagulant!

1842
01:45:08.838 --> 01:45:10.423
All vehicles. initiate pumps!

1843
01:45:10.507 --> 01:45:12.050
RC operational!

1844
01:45:12.133 --> 01:45:14.636
Okay! Raise output pressure
to the maximum output!

1845
01:45:14.719 --> 01:45:16.179
Target the mouth as much as possible!

1846
01:45:22.185 --> 01:45:25.355
Dosage. 20% has been administered.

1847
01:45:29.984 --> 01:45:32.904
<i>Dosage. 30% has been administered.</i>

1848
01:45:41.371 --> 01:45:44.040
Crane Platoon 1. Destroyed.

1849
01:45:57.262 --> 01:45:58.513
The dosage is working!

1850
01:45:58.596 --> 01:46:00.848
The target's movements are slowing down!

1851
01:46:00.932 --> 01:46:02.475
Now or never. We can't let it slip away.

1852
01:46:02.559 --> 01:46:03.851
All train bombs. now!

1853
01:46:26.416 --> 01:46:28.167
Gojira. It's fallen again!

1854
01:46:28.251 --> 01:46:30.295
Commander Tanba.
please send out the second platoon!

1855
01:46:30.378 --> 01:46:32.672
2nd and 3rd platoons. advance!

1856
01:46:32.755 --> 01:46:34.048
Freeze it once and for all!

1857
01:46:56.362 --> 01:46:58.615
All vehicles. administer all at once!

1858
01:47:04.162 --> 01:47:06.122
50% of the dosage has been administered!

1859
01:47:06.205 --> 01:47:07.957
The tanks up to number 20 are empty.

1860
01:47:08.041 --> 01:47:09.125
Roger.

1861
01:47:09.208 --> 01:47:11.294
Switch tanks to number 21 and above!

1862
01:47:13.838 --> 01:47:16.174
Dosage. 60% has been administered!

1863
01:47:30.647 --> 01:47:32.607
75% has been administered.

1864
01:47:32.690 --> 01:47:35.777
We've exceeded the projected
minimum dosage of blood coagulant.

1865
01:47:39.447 --> 01:47:41.491
90% has been administered!

1866
01:47:45.286 --> 01:47:46.829
100% has been administered.

1867
01:47:46.913 --> 01:47:48.539
We've reached the critical point!

1868
01:47:48.623 --> 01:47:51.167
The target's skin is stiffening!

1869
01:47:51.250 --> 01:47:53.002
Please follow the calculation.

1870
01:48:04.639 --> 01:48:06.432
Did it work?

1871
01:48:12.355 --> 01:48:13.856
<i>The target has resumed activity!</i>

1872
01:48:15.358 --> 01:48:17.151
<i>Everyone evacuate! Everyone evacuate!</i>

1873
01:48:17.235 --> 01:48:18.945
<i>All vehicles change positions! Hurry!</i>

1874
01:48:19.028 --> 01:48:21.656
<i>Special Construction 03.
all vehicles. maximum losses!</i>

1875
01:48:21.739 --> 01:48:23.574
<i>Abandon equipment
and evacuate to holding area!</i>

1876
01:48:36.254 --> 01:48:39.507
Chest temperature has dropped
to -196 degrees.

1877
01:48:41.175 --> 01:48:45.054
Gojira has been completely silenced.

1878
01:48:48.933 --> 01:48:52.311
Operation Yashiori has been completed.

1879
01:49:01.237 --> 01:49:02.947
Thank you.

1880
01:49:03.030 --> 01:49:04.365
You were remarkable.

1881
01:49:06.451 --> 01:49:08.619
That was too close.

1882
01:49:12.498 --> 01:49:15.001
Less than an hour left until launch.

1883
01:49:15.084 --> 01:49:16.961
That was too close for comfort.

1884
01:49:17.044 --> 01:49:18.921
It's all thanks
to the acting prime minister

1885
01:49:19.005 --> 01:49:21.048
for succeeding in convincing the French.

1886
01:49:28.639 --> 01:49:30.558
Everyone.

1887
01:49:31.476 --> 01:49:34.061
Take a look at this survey data.

1888
01:49:40.651 --> 01:49:42.612
Ah.

1889
01:49:42.695 --> 01:49:46.532
Gojira's new isotope
has a half-life of 20 days.

1890
01:49:46.657 --> 01:49:48.659
It'll reduce to less than half in a month.

1891
01:49:48.743 --> 01:49:50.328
Almost gone in two or three years.

1892
01:49:50.411 --> 01:49:53.539
Yes. With this there's hope
for a decontamination.

1893
01:49:53.623 --> 01:49:55.541
Hmm.

1894
01:49:58.294 --> 01:49:59.962
Thank goodness.

1895
01:50:11.265 --> 01:50:13.226
Good work.

1896
01:50:14.435 --> 01:50:19.148
Very soon. the Satomi Cabinet
will take full responsibility and resign.

1897
01:50:20.316 --> 01:50:22.777
And I suppose that falls nicely in line
with what you had planned.

1898
01:50:22.860 --> 01:50:24.278
It wasn't my idea.

1899
01:50:24.362 --> 01:50:26.864
It was Prime Minister Satomi's decision.

1900
01:50:34.413 --> 01:50:37.667
The capital and government
are now in ruins.

1901
01:50:37.750 --> 01:50:40.461
We'll rebuild them into
a functioning structure.

1902
01:50:42.380 --> 01:50:46.801
If the next provisional government passes
the bill on Giant Unidentified Life-Forms.

1903
01:50:46.884 --> 01:50:50.555
that'll be the time to dissolve the Diet.
and hold a general election.

1904
01:50:50.638 --> 01:50:54.934
A new cabinet to face 3.6 million refugees
and a dying country.

1905
01:50:55.017 --> 01:50:57.645
That's what we're gonna need
for the sake of our future.

1906
01:51:00.898 --> 01:51:05.444
Scrapping and building has always led
to our country's growth.

1907
01:51:07.321 --> 01:51:09.490
So we'll build back again.

1908
01:51:32.638 --> 01:51:34.974
The countdown was merely suspended.

1909
01:51:35.057 --> 01:51:38.519
but the moment Godzilla resumes activity.
it'll restart.

1910
01:51:38.603 --> 01:51:42.106
3.526 seconds to launch.

1911
01:51:42.982 --> 01:51:45.610
That was awfully lenient of you.

1912
01:51:46.235 --> 01:51:48.988
Something had to be done
to reassure the world.

1913
01:51:49.071 --> 01:51:52.366
Now Japan... no...

1914
01:51:52.450 --> 01:51:55.912
all of mankind must coexist with Gojira.

1915
01:51:57.914 --> 01:52:00.249
You leaked the data to France. didn't you?

1916
01:52:00.333 --> 01:52:04.003
France deserved to know
but also the rest of the world.

1917
01:52:04.086 --> 01:52:06.213
I broke a promise. but regret nothing.

1918
01:52:07.548 --> 01:52:10.718
I respect how you do whatever's necessary.

1919
01:52:10.801 --> 01:52:12.637
Don't quit.

1920
01:52:13.721 --> 01:52:15.264
You better not quit.

1921
01:52:18.559 --> 01:52:20.353
I have a clear vision for the future

1922
01:52:20.436 --> 01:52:23.397
where I'm the U.S. President
and you're the Prime Minister.

1923
01:52:23.481 --> 01:52:25.900
So I'd be your Japanese puppet.

1924
01:52:27.568 --> 01:52:31.280
The fact remains.
the casualties were high.

1925
01:52:31.364 --> 01:52:34.533
Accountability always comes with the job.

1926
01:52:35.451 --> 01:52:39.413
However a politician must decide
whether to own it or not.

1927
01:52:42.083 --> 01:52:44.502
I myself choose to own it.

1928
01:52:47.505 --> 01:52:51.133
Well. as Maki said...

1929
01:52:51.217 --> 01:52:53.928
do whatever you want.

1930
01:53:10.069 --> 01:53:12.863
But now's not the time to quit.

1931
01:53:15.533 --> 01:53:19.495
Especially since this crisis
is far from over.
